import FTQCLib.Carrier.Protocol
import FTQCLib.Carrier.ConditionFloor
import FTQCLib.Carrier.PrecisionGauge
import FTQCLib.Carrier.FinAppend
import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Braided.Basic

/-!
# The frame as a monoidal category

The statement of T46 (`docs/TARGETS.md`; `docs/framing/T46.md`; `docs/fidelity/T46.md`). Objects are
register sizes, a type wrapping `ℕ` (`FrameCategory.Obj`). A morphism `n → m` is a `StateEq` class
of `KernelSumState (n + m)`, the quotient by `stateSetoid` (`FrameCategory.Hom`), the zero class
included: the first `n` free bits are the inputs `x`, the last `m` the outputs `y`, and a class is
its amplitude `f(x, y) = amp F (Fin.append x y)`, the matrix entry `⟨y|F|x⟩` unnormalised (D3).
A class has no precision and no presentation, so every law below is an equality of classes.

**Composition** is the contraction `(g ∘ f)(x, z) = Σ_y f(x, y)·g(y, z)` (`contractAmp`, the
referee), built on carrier states as the framing note's construction C (`compState`): the two
factors are brought to one precision (R7) and appended, the register is read with the outer bits
first and the shared pairs last (`compLayout`), and each shared pair `(y, y′)` is contracted
(`contractPair`): a CNOT `y → y′` then `restrictZ y′ 0`, which is the conditioning on `Z_yZ_{y′}`
at outcome `0` with the support cut to the slice and the determined copy `y′` dropped; then H on
`y` and `restrictZ y 0`, which sums `y` out at `(1/√2)·Σ_y`; and the scale `√2`, which restores
the plain sum. `dropFreeBit` alone evaluates the shared bit at one value and is not composition
(fidelity note, Claim 5). Two things make the composite a function of the two amplitudes, so that
composition is well defined on classes (`comp_stateEq_congr`). Each factor enters through a carrier
presentation of its amplitude, chosen (`carrierRep`): a class may have presentations that are not
carrier states, on which the frozen theorems `amp_run` and `amp_restrictZ` say nothing, and every
nonzero amplitude has a carrier presentation (`exists_carrier_of_amp_ne_zero`). And when the
contraction is zero the composite is the zero presentation (Comfort's empty relation, D10):
otherwise every intermediate state is nonzero, since each step is linear, so it is a carrier
state where the theorems apply (`amp_comp`, `isCarrier_comp`).

**The identity** `n → n` is `δ_{x = y}` (`idState`): the Bell floor of `n` pairs `(i, n + i)` at
scale `1` and height `0`, whose Lagrangian is generated by `X_iX_{n+i}` and `Z_iZ_{n+i}` (`idL`);
at `n = 1` it is `bellState`. It is not the normalised Bell state, whose composite with `f` is
`f/√2` (framing note, case I1). **The tensor** is `Fin.append` of the two presentations followed by
the middle swap (`middleSwap`, `tensorState`), so that a morphism `n + n′ → m + m′` reads its bits
as `(x, x′, y, y′)`; the bare `Fin.append` reads them as `(x, y, x′, y′)`, under which
`id₁ ⊗ id₁ ≠ id₂` (case I2). **The symmetry** `n + m → m + n` is the identity with its output half
flipped (`swapState`), with its involution `swap_swap`, its naturality `swap_natural` and the
hexagon `swap_hexagon`; the interchange law is `tensor_comp`. The associator and the unitors are
casts of identities (`castHom`), since the objects add strictly.

**Letters as morphisms.** A gate word on `N` bits acts on the output half of the identity on `N`
pairs through a `Fin.natAdd N` shift (`natAddWord`, `wordState`), the identity first lifted to the
word's precision by R7 (`idAt`): without the lift a diagonal letter at another precision is left as
the identity (case P2). A conditioning letter is `conditionOutcome` of the shifted Pauli on that
lifted identity, a morphism `N → N + 1` with the outcome bit last (`conditionState`), as in T14.
A protocol's morphism is the composite of its letters' (`protocolHom`), and a carrier state on `n`
bits is a morphism `0 → n` through the cast `0 + n = n`, which keeps `amp` (`ofState`). The
statement `interpret_eq_comp` is that T14's interpretation of a protocol on a carrier state at the
protocol's precision is the composite of the state with the protocol's morphism, so that every
T14 term is a composite of its letters.

**The corpus.** Comfort's props of linear, Lagrangian and affine relations have morphisms `n → m`
as subspaces of the sum of the two sides, relational composition and the direct sum as the tensor;
an affine relation may be empty; the monoidal structure of the doubling reorders by `1 ⊕ σ ⊕ 1`,
the middle swap; the forgetful functor is strong symmetric monoidal. Those are the shapes stated
here on amplitudes; no corpus unit states the contraction, the identity at scale `1` or the letters,
which are the frame's own (fidelity note). The paper's equivalence with stabilizer theory is for
odd primes and up to scalars, and is not claimed.

Everything here is frame-pure (decision D5). No `FTQCLib.Hilbert` module is imported.

## Main definitions

* `castBits`, `scaleBy`, `reindexFreeBits`, `appendState` — a cast of the register, a scale, a
  reindexing of the free bits, and two presentations appended at one precision.
* `contractPair`, `contractShared`, `carrierRep`, `compState` — one shared pair contracted, all of
  them, a carrier presentation of an amplitude, and composition on presentations.
* `idState`, `tensorState`, `swapState`, `zeroState` — the identity, the tensor, the symmetry and
  the zero presentation; `natAddWord`, `natAddPauli`, `idAt`, `wordState`, `conditionState` — the
  letters as presentations.
* `FrameCategory.Obj`, `FrameCategory.Hom`, `FrameCategory.comp`, `FrameCategory.id`,
  `FrameCategory.tensor`, `FrameCategory.swap`, `FrameCategory.zero`, `FrameCategory.castHom` —
  the category on classes; `FrameCategory.ofState`, `FrameCategory.wordHom`,
  `FrameCategory.conditionHom`, `FrameCategory.protocolHom` — states and T14's terms as morphisms.

## Main results

* `comp_stateEq_congr`, `isCarrier_comp`, `amp_comp` — composition respects `StateEq` in both
  arguments, a nonzero composite is a carrier state, and the composite's amplitude is the
  contraction, for every pair of presentations (T46.3.1).
* `amp_idState`, `amp_tensorState`, `amp_swapState`, `amp_wordState`, `amp_conditionState` — the
  referees of the identity, the tensor, the symmetry and the letters (T46.3.1).
* `exists_carrier_of_amp_ne_zero` — every nonzero amplitude of a `KernelSumState` is a carrier
  state's: the Lagrangian is replaced by one with the same X-shadow, the precision lifted (T46.3.1).
* `shadowLagrangian` with `map_xProj_shadowLagrangian`, `isStabilizer_shadowLagrangian`,
  `orthogonal_shadowLagrangian_le` — the Lagrangian `{X^v Z^u : v ∈ V, u ∈ V^⊥}` with X-shadow `V`,
  public since entry 2026-10-02c (T47.3 had restated them).
* `comp_assoc`, `id_comp`, `comp_id`, `tensor_comp`, `tensor_id`, `swap_swap`, `swap_natural`,
  `swap_hexagon`, `tensor_assoc`, `tensor_id_left`, `tensor_id_right` — the laws, on classes
  (T46.3.2; the last three added by restatement, docs/STEPS.md, entry 2026-10-01p).
* `FrameCategory.category`, `FrameCategory.monoidalCategory`, `FrameCategory.symmetricCategory` —
  the frame as Mathlib's `Category`, `MonoidalCategory` and `SymmetricCategory` on `Obj`, so that
  T47 is stated for a Mathlib symmetric monoidal category (T46.3.2; entry 2026-10-01p).
* `interpret_eq_comp` — T14's interpretation is the composite of the letters' morphisms (T46.3.3).

## Implementation notes

* `comp` and `tensor` are `Quotient.lift₂` of `compState` and `tensorState`, with the congruences
  `comp_stateEq_congr` and `tensor_stateEq_congr`; `compState` reads its factors only through
  their amplitudes, so the first is immediate and the work of T46.3.1 is `amp_comp`.
* The register sizes `n + (m + k)` and `(n + m) + k`, and `0 + n` and `n`, are equal only
  propositionally, so the tensor, the symmetry, the contraction and the embedding of states
  reindex through `castBits`, the transport along the equality, which keeps `amp` (`amp_castBits`);
  `n + (k + 1)` and `(n + k) + 1` agree by definition, so `protocolHom` needs no cast.
* `idAt N M` is the identity lifted to `max 1 M`, so that it is total; on a carrier state the
  protocol's precision is positive, and `amp_wordState` takes `1 ≤ M`, which `amp_run` needs.
-/

namespace FTQCLib.Frame.Walkthrough

open FTQCLib FTQCLib.Pauli FTQCLib.Hierarchy FTQCLib.Stabilizer

/-! ## Casts, scales and reindexings of a presentation -/

-- designed double: blindCastState (the blind restatement's own; entry 2026-10-02d)
/-- A presentation read on a register of the same size: the transport along `h`. -/
def castBits {N N' : ℕ} (h : N = N') (S : KernelSumState N) : KernelSumState N' := h ▸ S

/-- The cast keeps the amplitude, read through `Fin.cast`. -/
theorem amp_castBits {N N' : ℕ} (h : N = N') (S : KernelSumState N) :
    amp (castBits h S) = fun w => amp S (w ∘ Fin.cast h) := by
  subst h
  rfl

/-- The cast respects `StateEq`. -/
theorem castBits_stateEq_congr {N N' : ℕ} (h : N = N') {S T : KernelSumState N}
    (hST : StateEq S T) : StateEq (castBits h S) (castBits h T) := by
  unfold StateEq at hST ⊢
  rw [amp_castBits, amp_castBits, hST]

/-- The scale multiplied by `z`; the support and the exponent are unchanged. -/
def scaleBy {N : ℕ} (z : ℂ) (S : KernelSumState N) : KernelSumState N :=
  { S with c := z * S.c }

/-- **A reindexing of the free bits** along an equivalence of registers of one size: old bit `i`
is read at new position `e i`. It is `permuteFreeBits` by the equivalence read as a permutation,
then the cast. -/
noncomputable def reindexFreeBits {N N' : ℕ} (h : N = N') (e : Fin N ≃ Fin N')
    (S : KernelSumState N) : KernelSumState N' :=
  castBits h (permuteFreeBits (e.trans (finCongr h.symm)) S)

/-- The amplitude of a reindexing is the input's precomposed with `e`. -/
theorem amp_reindexFreeBits {N N' : ℕ} (h : N = N') (e : Fin N ≃ Fin N')
    (S : KernelSumState N) : amp (reindexFreeBits h e S) = fun w => amp S (w ∘ e) := by
  funext w
  unfold reindexFreeBits
  rw [amp_castBits, amp_permuteFreeBits]
  rfl

/-! ## Two presentations appended at one precision -/

/-- The first `N` qubits of a Pauli on `N + N'`. -/
def pauliLeft (N N' : ℕ) : Pauli (N + N') →ₗ[ZMod 2] Pauli N where
  toFun p := ⟨p.X ∘ Fin.castAdd N', p.Z ∘ Fin.castAdd N'⟩
  map_add' _ _ := rfl
  map_smul' _ _ := rfl

/-- The last `N'` qubits of a Pauli on `N + N'`. -/
def pauliRight (N N' : ℕ) : Pauli (N + N') →ₗ[ZMod 2] Pauli N' where
  toFun p := ⟨p.X ∘ Fin.natAdd N, p.Z ∘ Fin.natAdd N⟩
  map_add' _ _ := rfl
  map_smul' _ _ := rfl

/-- The variables of the first exponent, read on the appended register: its free block to the
first `N` free bits, its bound block to the first `h` bound bits. -/
def appendVarLeft (N N' h h' : ℕ) : Fin (N + h) → Fin ((N + N') + (h + h')) :=
  Fin.append (fun i : Fin N => Fin.castAdd (h + h') (Fin.castAdd N' i))
    (fun y : Fin h => Fin.natAdd (N + N') (Fin.castAdd h' y))

/-- The variables of the second exponent, read on the appended register: its free block to the
last `N'` free bits, its bound block to the last `h'` bound bits. -/
def appendVarRight (N N' h h' : ℕ) : Fin (N' + h') → Fin ((N + N') + (h + h')) :=
  Fin.append (fun i : Fin N' => Fin.castAdd (h + h') (Fin.natAdd N i))
    (fun y : Fin h' => Fin.natAdd (N + N') (Fin.natAdd h y))

/-- **Two presentations appended**, at the larger of their precisions (R7): the exponents lifted
and added on the disjoint variables, the heights added, the scales multiplied, the Lagrangian
`L ⊕ L'` and the offset `Fin.append x₀ x₀'`. Its amplitude at `Fin.append u v` is
`amp F u · amp G v`. -/
noncomputable def appendState {N N' : ℕ} (F : KernelSumState N) (G : KernelSumState N') :
    KernelSumState (N + N') where
  m := max F.m G.m
  h := F.h + G.h
  Q := MvPolynomial.rename (appendVarLeft N N' F.h G.h)
        (FTQCLib.Hilbert.liftTo (max F.m G.m) (le_max_left F.m G.m) F.Q)
      + MvPolynomial.rename (appendVarRight N N' F.h G.h)
        (FTQCLib.Hilbert.liftTo (max F.m G.m) (le_max_right F.m G.m) G.Q)
  c := F.c * G.c
  L := Submodule.comap (pauliLeft N N') F.L ⊓ Submodule.comap (pauliRight N N') G.L
  x₀ := Fin.append F.x₀ G.x₀

/-- The first exponent's variables read the first free block and the first bound block. -/
private theorem append_comp_appendVarLeft {N N' h h' : ℕ} (w : Fin (N + N') → ZMod 2)
    (y₁ : Fin h → ZMod 2) (y₂ : Fin h' → ZMod 2) :
    Fin.append w (Fin.append y₁ y₂) ∘ appendVarLeft N N' h h'
      = Fin.append (w ∘ Fin.castAdd N') y₁ := by
  funext i
  refine Fin.addCases (fun i => ?_) (fun i => ?_) i
  · simp only [Function.comp_apply, appendVarLeft, Fin.append_left]
  · simp only [Function.comp_apply, appendVarLeft, Fin.append_left, Fin.append_right]

/-- The second exponent's variables read the last free block and the last bound block. -/
private theorem append_comp_appendVarRight {N N' h h' : ℕ} (w : Fin (N + N') → ZMod 2)
    (y₁ : Fin h → ZMod 2) (y₂ : Fin h' → ZMod 2) :
    Fin.append w (Fin.append y₁ y₂) ∘ appendVarRight N N' h h'
      = Fin.append (w ∘ Fin.natAdd N) y₂ := by
  funext i
  refine Fin.addCases (fun i => ?_) (fun i => ?_) i
  · simp only [Function.comp_apply, appendVarRight, Fin.append_left]
  · simp only [Function.comp_apply, appendVarRight, Fin.append_right]

/-- The phase of a renamed exponent is the phase read through the renaming. -/
private theorem realPhase_rename {K K' m : ℕ} (f : Fin K → Fin K') (P : DiagPhase K m)
    (v : Fin K' → ZMod 2) :
    DiagPhase.realPhase (MvPolynomial.rename f P) v = DiagPhase.realPhase P (v ∘ f) := by
  unfold DiagPhase.realPhase
  rw [DiagPhase.eval_rename]

/-- A sum over the words of `h + h'` bits is a double sum over the two blocks. -/
private theorem sum_append_split {h h' : ℕ} (f : (Fin (h + h') → ZMod 2) → ℂ) :
    ∑ y, f y = ∑ y₁ : Fin h → ZMod 2, ∑ y₂ : Fin h' → ZMod 2, f (Fin.append y₁ y₂) := by
  rw [← Fintype.sum_prod_type']
  exact (Fintype.sum_equiv (Fin.appendEquiv h h') _ _ (fun _ => rfl)).symm

/-- On support, the appended presentation's amplitude is the product of the two: the exponents
are added on disjoint variables, so the sum over the bound bits factors. -/
private theorem ampCore_appendState {N N' : ℕ} (F : KernelSumState N) (G : KernelSumState N')
    (w : Fin (N + N') → ZMod 2) :
    ampCore (appendState F G).m (appendState F G).h (appendState F G).Q (appendState F G).c w
      = ampCore F.m F.h F.Q F.c (w ∘ Fin.castAdd N')
        * ampCore G.m G.h G.Q G.c (w ∘ Fin.natAdd N) := by
  unfold ampCore
  change (F.c * G.c) / (Real.sqrt 2 : ℂ) ^ (F.h + G.h) * ∑ y : Fin (F.h + G.h) → ZMod 2,
      Complex.exp (Complex.I * (DiagPhase.realPhase
        (MvPolynomial.rename (appendVarLeft N N' F.h G.h)
          (FTQCLib.Hilbert.liftTo (max F.m G.m) (le_max_left F.m G.m) F.Q)
        + MvPolynomial.rename (appendVarRight N N' F.h G.h)
          (FTQCLib.Hilbert.liftTo (max F.m G.m) (le_max_right F.m G.m) G.Q)) (Fin.append w y) : ℂ))
    = _
  have hterm : ∀ (y₁ : Fin F.h → ZMod 2) (y₂ : Fin G.h → ZMod 2),
      Complex.exp (Complex.I * (DiagPhase.realPhase
        (MvPolynomial.rename (appendVarLeft N N' F.h G.h)
          (FTQCLib.Hilbert.liftTo (max F.m G.m) (le_max_left F.m G.m) F.Q)
        + MvPolynomial.rename (appendVarRight N N' F.h G.h)
          (FTQCLib.Hilbert.liftTo (max F.m G.m) (le_max_right F.m G.m) G.Q))
          (Fin.append w (Fin.append y₁ y₂)) : ℂ))
      = Complex.exp (Complex.I
            * (DiagPhase.realPhase F.Q (Fin.append (w ∘ Fin.castAdd N') y₁) : ℂ))
        * Complex.exp (Complex.I
            * (DiagPhase.realPhase G.Q (Fin.append (w ∘ Fin.natAdd N) y₂) : ℂ)) := by
    intro y₁ y₂
    rw [exp_realPhase_add, realPhase_rename, realPhase_rename, append_comp_appendVarLeft,
      append_comp_appendVarRight, FTQCLib.Hilbert.liftTo_realPhase,
      FTQCLib.Hilbert.liftTo_realPhase]
  rw [sum_append_split,
    Finset.sum_congr rfl fun y₁ _ => Finset.sum_congr rfl fun y₂ _ => hterm y₁ y₂,
    pow_add, mul_mul_mul_comm, Finset.sum_mul_sum, div_mul_div_comm]

/-- A word is on the appended support exactly when its two halves are on the two supports. -/
private theorem support_appendState_iff {N N' : ℕ} (F : KernelSumState N)
    (G : KernelSumState N') (w : Fin (N + N') → ZMod 2) :
    (∃ p ∈ (appendState F G).L, w = (appendState F G).x₀ + p.X)
      ↔ (∃ p ∈ F.L, w ∘ Fin.castAdd N' = F.x₀ + p.X)
        ∧ (∃ q ∈ G.L, w ∘ Fin.natAdd N = G.x₀ + q.X) := by
  have hx₀ : (appendState F G).x₀ = Fin.append F.x₀ G.x₀ := rfl
  rw [hx₀]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨p, hp, rfl⟩
    refine ⟨⟨pauliLeft N N' p, (Submodule.mem_inf.mp hp).1, ?_⟩,
      ⟨pauliRight N N' p, (Submodule.mem_inf.mp hp).2, ?_⟩⟩
    · funext i
      simp only [Function.comp_apply, Pi.add_apply, Fin.append_left, pauliLeft,
        LinearMap.coe_mk, AddHom.coe_mk]
    · funext i
      simp only [Function.comp_apply, Pi.add_apply, Fin.append_right, pauliRight,
        LinearMap.coe_mk, AddHom.coe_mk]
  · rintro ⟨⟨p, hp, hpw⟩, ⟨q, hq, hqw⟩⟩
    let r : Pauli (N + N') := ⟨Fin.append p.X q.X, Fin.append p.Z q.Z⟩
    have hrl : pauliLeft N N' r = p := by
      apply Pauli.ext <;> funext i <;>
        simp only [r, pauliLeft, LinearMap.coe_mk, AddHom.coe_mk, Function.comp_apply,
          Fin.append_left]
    have hrr : pauliRight N N' r = q := by
      apply Pauli.ext <;> funext i <;>
        simp only [r, pauliRight, LinearMap.coe_mk, AddHom.coe_mk, Function.comp_apply,
          Fin.append_right]
    refine ⟨r, Submodule.mem_inf.mpr ⟨?_, ?_⟩, ?_⟩
    · change pauliLeft N N' r ∈ F.L
      rw [hrl]
      exact hp
    · change pauliRight N N' r ∈ G.L
      rw [hrr]
      exact hq
    · funext i
      refine Fin.addCases (fun i => ?_) (fun i => ?_) i
      · have h := congrFun hpw i
        simp only [Function.comp_apply, Pi.add_apply] at h
        simp only [Pi.add_apply, Fin.append_left, r, h]
      · have h := congrFun hqw i
        simp only [Function.comp_apply, Pi.add_apply] at h
        simp only [Pi.add_apply, Fin.append_right, r, h]

/-- **The amplitude of two presentations appended** is the product of their amplitudes at the two
halves of the word. Proved at T46.3.1. -/
theorem amp_appendState {N N' : ℕ} (F : KernelSumState N) (G : KernelSumState N') :
    amp (appendState F G) = fun w => amp F (w ∘ Fin.castAdd N') * amp G (w ∘ Fin.natAdd N) := by
  funext w
  by_cases hw : ∃ p ∈ (appendState F G).L, w = (appendState F G).x₀ + p.X
  · obtain ⟨hF, hG⟩ := (support_appendState_iff F G w).mp hw
    rw [amp_pos hw, amp_pos hF, amp_pos hG]
    exact ampCore_appendState F G w
  · rw [amp_neg hw]
    by_cases hF : ∃ p ∈ F.L, w ∘ Fin.castAdd N' = F.x₀ + p.X
    · have hG : ¬ ∃ q ∈ G.L, w ∘ Fin.natAdd N = G.x₀ + q.X :=
        fun hG => hw ((support_appendState_iff F G w).mpr ⟨hF, hG⟩)
      rw [amp_neg hG, mul_zero]
    · rw [amp_neg hF, zero_mul]

/-! ## The zero presentation and a carrier presentation of an amplitude -/

/-- The zero presentation: scale `0`, so amplitude `0` (`amp_c_zero`); not a carrier state (D10). -/
noncomputable def zeroState (N : ℕ) : KernelSumState N := ⟨1, 0, 0, 0, ⊥, 0⟩

open Classical in
/-- **A carrier presentation of an amplitude**, chosen; the zero presentation when none exists,
which by `exists_carrier_of_amp_ne_zero` is exactly when the amplitude is zero. A function of the
amplitude alone, so that what is built on it is well defined on `StateEq` classes. -/
noncomputable def carrierRep {N : ℕ} (φ : (Fin N → ZMod 2) → ℂ) : KernelSumState N :=
  if h : ∃ S : KernelSumState N, IsCarrier S ∧ amp S = φ then Classical.choose h else zeroState N

/-! ## Contracting the shared pairs -/

/-- The referee of one shared pair: the two bits, `a` and the last, take one value, summed over.
-/
noncomputable def contractPairAmp {K : ℕ} (a : Fin (K + 1)) (φ : (Fin (K + 1 + 1) → ZMod 2) → ℂ) :
    (Fin K → ZMod 2) → ℂ :=
  fun w => ∑ β : ZMod 2, φ (Fin.snoc (Fin.insertNth a β w) β : Fin (K + 1 + 1) → ZMod 2)

/-- **One shared pair contracted**, the bit `a` and the last bit of a register `K + 2`: a CNOT
`a → last` then `restrictZ last 0`, which is the conditioning on `Z_aZ_last` at outcome `0` with
the support cut to the slice `w_a = w_last` and the determined copy dropped; then H on `a` and
`restrictZ a 0`, which sums `a` out at `(1/√2)·Σ_β`; then the scale `√2`, which restores the plain
sum. Never `dropFreeBit` alone on a shared bit. -/
noncomputable def contractPair {K : ℕ} (a : Fin (K + 1)) (T : KernelSumState (K + 1 + 1)) :
    KernelSumState K :=
  scaleBy (Real.sqrt 2 : ℂ)
    (restrictZ a 0
      (run (m := T.m) [GateLetter.hadamard a]
        (restrictZ (Fin.last (K + 1)) 0
          (run (m := T.m)
            [GateLetter.cnot (Fin.castSucc a) (Fin.last (K + 1)) (Fin.castSucc_lt_last a).ne]
            T))))

/-- The referee of all `m` shared pairs: the register `(w, y, y′)` with `y′ = y`, summed over `y`.
-/
noncomputable def contractSharedAmp (R m : ℕ) (φ : (Fin (R + (m + m)) → ZMod 2) → ℂ) :
    (Fin R → ZMod 2) → ℂ :=
  fun w => ∑ y : Fin m → ZMod 2, φ (Fin.append w (Fin.append y y))

/-- **All shared pairs contracted**, last pair first, on a register `(w, y₀ … y_{m-1}, y′₀ …
y′_{m-1})`: the last pair is `(y_{m-1}, y′_{m-1})`, bit `R + (m − 1)` and the last bit. -/
noncomputable def contractShared (R : ℕ) : (m : ℕ) → KernelSumState (R + (m + m)) → KernelSumState R
  | 0, T => T
  | m + 1, T => contractShared R m (contractPair ⟨R + m, by omega⟩ (castBits (by omega) T))

/-! ## Composition on presentations -/

/-- **The referee of composition** (D5): the contraction `(g ∘ f)(x, z) = Σ_y f(x, y)·g(y, z)`,
the matrix product in the reading `f(x, y) = ⟨y|F|x⟩`. -/
noncomputable def contractAmp (n m p : ℕ) (f : (Fin (n + m) → ZMod 2) → ℂ)
    (g : (Fin (m + p) → ZMod 2) → ℂ) : (Fin (n + p) → ZMod 2) → ℂ :=
  fun w => ∑ y : Fin m → ZMod 2,
    f (Fin.append (w ∘ Fin.castAdd p) y) * g (Fin.append y (w ∘ Fin.natAdd n))

/-- The register `(x, y, y′, z)` of `F : n → m` appended to `G : m → p`, read as `(x, z, y, y′)`:
the outer bits first, the shared pairs last. -/
def compLayout (n m p : ℕ) : Fin ((n + m) + (m + p)) ≃ Fin ((n + p) + (m + m)) :=
  finSumFinEquiv.symm.trans
    ((Equiv.sumCongr finSumFinEquiv.symm finSumFinEquiv.symm).trans
      ((Equiv.sumCongr (Equiv.refl (Fin n ⊕ Fin m)) (Equiv.sumComm (Fin m) (Fin p))).trans
        ((Equiv.sumSumSumComm (Fin n) (Fin m) (Fin p) (Fin m)).trans
          ((Equiv.sumCongr finSumFinEquiv finSumFinEquiv).trans finSumFinEquiv))))

-- source: papers/categorical_qm/
-- Comfort_2021_graphical_calculus_lagrangian_relations_2105.06244 definition:h995b6231ad87
-- source: papers/categorical_qm/
-- Comfort_2021_graphical_calculus_lagrangian_relations_2105.06244 definition:h7963d1a59afa
open Classical in
/-- **Composition on presentations** (the framing note's construction C): the corpus's relational
composition, an existential over the shared side, read on amplitudes as the contraction. When the
contraction of the two amplitudes is zero, the zero presentation (the empty relation). Otherwise
the carrier presentations of the two amplitudes are appended at one precision, the register is
read with the shared pairs last, and the pairs are contracted. A function of the two amplitudes
alone. -/
noncomputable def compState {n m p : ℕ} (F : KernelSumState (n + m)) (G : KernelSumState (m + p)) :
    KernelSumState (n + p) :=
  if contractAmp n m p (amp F) (amp G) = 0 then zeroState (n + p)
  else contractShared (n + p) m
    (reindexFreeBits (by omega) (compLayout n m p)
      (appendState (carrierRep (amp F)) (carrierRep (amp G))))

/-- **Composition respects `StateEq` in both arguments.** `compState` reads its factors through
their amplitudes alone. Stated here; the step T46.3.1 owns it. -/
theorem comp_stateEq_congr {n m p : ℕ} {F F' : KernelSumState (n + m)}
    {G G' : KernelSumState (m + p)} (hF : StateEq F F') (hG : StateEq G G') :
    StateEq (compState F G) (compState F' G') := by
  unfold StateEq at hF hG
  unfold compState
  rw [hF, hG]
  exact StateEq.refl _

/-! ## The identity, the tensor and the symmetry on presentations -/

/-- The Lagrangian of the identity on `n` pairs `(i, n + i)`: generated by `X_iX_{n+i}` and
`Z_iZ_{n+i}`; at `n = 1` it is `bellL`. -/
def idL (n : ℕ) : Submodule (ZMod 2) (Pauli (n + n)) where
  carrier := {p | ∀ i : Fin n,
    p.X (Fin.castAdd n i) = p.X (Fin.natAdd n i) ∧ p.Z (Fin.castAdd n i) = p.Z (Fin.natAdd n i)}
  zero_mem' := fun _ => ⟨rfl, rfl⟩
  add_mem' := fun hp hq i => ⟨by simp [(hp i).1, (hq i).1], by simp [(hp i).2, (hq i).2]⟩
  smul_mem' := fun c _ hp i => ⟨by simp [(hp i).1], by simp [(hp i).2]⟩

/-- **The identity** `n → n`: the Bell floor of `n` pairs `(i, n + i)` at scale `1` and height `0`,
with amplitude `δ_{x = y}`; `bellState` at `n = 1`. Not the normalised Bell state. -/
noncomputable def idState (n : ℕ) : KernelSumState (n + n) where
  m := 1
  h := 0
  Q := 0
  c := 1
  L := idL n
  x₀ := 0

-- source: papers/categorical_qm/
-- Comfort_2021_graphical_calculus_lagrangian_relations_2105.06244 equation:h58cc1b72e2a6
/-- **The middle swap**: the register `(x, y, x′, y′)` of two presentations appended, read as
`(x, x′, y, y′)`; the corpus's `1 ⊕ σ ⊕ 1` in the monoidal structure of the doubling. -/
def middleSwap (n m n' m' : ℕ) : Fin ((n + m) + (n' + m')) ≃ Fin ((n + n') + (m + m')) :=
  finSumFinEquiv.symm.trans
    ((Equiv.sumCongr finSumFinEquiv.symm finSumFinEquiv.symm).trans
      ((Equiv.sumSumSumComm (Fin n) (Fin m) (Fin n') (Fin m')).trans
        ((Equiv.sumCongr finSumFinEquiv finSumFinEquiv).trans finSumFinEquiv)))

-- source: papers/categorical_qm/
-- Comfort_2021_graphical_calculus_lagrangian_relations_2105.06244 definition:h995b6231ad87
/-- **The tensor on presentations**: `Fin.append` at one precision followed by the middle swap,
so that a morphism `n + n′ → m + m′` reads its bits as `(x, x′, y, y′)`; the corpus's direct sum.
-/
noncomputable def tensorState {n m n' m' : ℕ} (F : KernelSumState (n + m))
    (G : KernelSumState (n' + m')) : KernelSumState ((n + n') + (m + m')) :=
  reindexFreeBits (Nat.add_add_add_comm n m n' m') (middleSwap n m n' m') (appendState F G)

/-- The first factor of the tensor reads `(x, y)` of the register `(x, x′, y, y′)`. -/
private theorem middleSwap_castAdd {n m n' m' : ℕ} (v : Fin ((n + n') + (m + m')) → ZMod 2) :
    (v ∘ middleSwap n m n' m') ∘ Fin.castAdd (n' + m')
      = Fin.append (v ∘ Fin.castAdd (m + m') ∘ Fin.castAdd n')
          (v ∘ Fin.natAdd (n + n') ∘ Fin.castAdd m') := by
  funext i
  refine Fin.addCases (fun i => ?_) (fun i => ?_) i
  · simp only [middleSwap, Equiv.coe_trans, Function.comp_apply, finSumFinEquiv_symm_apply_castAdd,
      Equiv.sumCongr_apply, Sum.map_inl, Equiv.sumSumSumComm_apply, Equiv.sumComm_apply,
      Equiv.sumAssoc_symm_apply_inl, Equiv.sumAssoc_apply_inl_inl, id_eq,
      finSumFinEquiv_apply_left, Fin.append_left]
  · simp only [middleSwap, Equiv.coe_trans, Function.comp_apply, finSumFinEquiv_symm_apply_castAdd,
      Equiv.sumCongr_apply, Sum.map_inl, finSumFinEquiv_symm_apply_natAdd,
      Equiv.sumSumSumComm_apply, Equiv.sumComm_apply, Equiv.sumAssoc_symm_apply_inl,
      Equiv.sumAssoc_apply_inl_inr, Sum.map_inr, Sum.swap_inl, Equiv.sumAssoc_symm_apply_inr_inr,
      finSumFinEquiv_apply_left, finSumFinEquiv_apply_right, Fin.append_right]

/-- The second factor of the tensor reads `(x′, y′)` of the register `(x, x′, y, y′)`. -/
private theorem middleSwap_natAdd {n m n' m' : ℕ} (v : Fin ((n + n') + (m + m')) → ZMod 2) :
    (v ∘ middleSwap n m n' m') ∘ Fin.natAdd (n + m)
      = Fin.append (v ∘ Fin.castAdd (m + m') ∘ Fin.natAdd n)
          (v ∘ Fin.natAdd (n + n') ∘ Fin.natAdd m) := by
  funext i
  refine Fin.addCases (fun i => ?_) (fun i => ?_) i
  · simp only [middleSwap, Equiv.coe_trans, Function.comp_apply, finSumFinEquiv_symm_apply_natAdd,
      Equiv.sumCongr_apply, Sum.map_inr, finSumFinEquiv_symm_apply_castAdd,
      Equiv.sumSumSumComm_apply, Equiv.sumComm_apply, Equiv.sumAssoc_symm_apply_inr_inl,
      Sum.map_inl, Equiv.sumAssoc_apply_inr, Sum.swap_inr, Equiv.sumAssoc_apply_inl_inl,
      finSumFinEquiv_apply_right, finSumFinEquiv_apply_left, Fin.append_left]
  · simp only [middleSwap, Equiv.coe_trans, Function.comp_apply, finSumFinEquiv_symm_apply_natAdd,
      Equiv.sumCongr_apply, Sum.map_inr, Equiv.sumSumSumComm_apply, Equiv.sumComm_apply,
      Equiv.sumAssoc_symm_apply_inr_inr, id_eq, Equiv.sumAssoc_apply_inr,
      finSumFinEquiv_apply_right, Fin.append_right]

/-- **The amplitude of the tensor** at `(x, x′, y, y′)` is `f(x, y)·g(x′, y′)`: the first factor
reads the first `n` inputs and the first `m` outputs, the second the rest. Proved at T46.3.1. -/
theorem amp_tensorState {n m n' m' : ℕ} (F : KernelSumState (n + m))
    (G : KernelSumState (n' + m')) :
    amp (tensorState F G) = fun w =>
      amp F (Fin.append (w ∘ Fin.castAdd (m + m') ∘ Fin.castAdd n')
          (w ∘ Fin.natAdd (n + n') ∘ Fin.castAdd m'))
        * amp G (Fin.append (w ∘ Fin.castAdd (m + m') ∘ Fin.natAdd n)
          (w ∘ Fin.natAdd (n + n') ∘ Fin.natAdd m)) := by
  funext w
  unfold tensorState
  rw [amp_reindexFreeBits, amp_appendState]
  change amp F ((w ∘ middleSwap n m n' m') ∘ Fin.castAdd (n' + m'))
      * amp G ((w ∘ middleSwap n m n' m') ∘ Fin.natAdd (n + m)) = _
  rw [middleSwap_castAdd, middleSwap_natAdd]

/-- The tensor respects `StateEq` in both arguments, by `amp_tensorState`. -/
theorem tensor_stateEq_congr {n m n' m' : ℕ} {F F' : KernelSumState (n + m)}
    {G G' : KernelSumState (n' + m')} (hF : StateEq F F') (hG : StateEq G G') :
    StateEq (tensorState F G) (tensorState F' G') := by
  unfold StateEq at hF hG ⊢
  rw [amp_tensorState, amp_tensorState, hF, hG]

-- source: papers/categorical_qm/
-- Comfort_2021_graphical_calculus_lagrangian_relations_2105.06244 lemma:lemma:strong
/-- **The symmetry on presentations** `n + m → m + n`: the identity on `n + m` pairs with its
output half flipped by `finAddFlip`, so that the input `(x₁, x₂)` is sent to `(x₂, x₁)`. -/
noncomputable def swapState (n m : ℕ) : KernelSumState ((n + m) + (m + n)) :=
  reindexFreeBits (by omega)
    (finSumFinEquiv.symm.trans
      ((Equiv.sumCongr (Equiv.refl (Fin (n + m))) finAddFlip).trans finSumFinEquiv))
    (idState (n + m))

/-! ## The letters as presentations -/

/-- A letter on `N` bits, shifted onto the output half of `N + N` by `Fin.natAdd N`. -/
noncomputable def natAddLetter (N : ℕ) {M : ℕ} : GateLetter N M → GateLetter (N + N) M
  | .hadamard k => .hadamard (Fin.natAdd N k)
  | .diagonal D => .diagonal (MvPolynomial.rename (Fin.natAdd N) D)
  | .cnot i j hij => .cnot (Fin.natAdd N i) (Fin.natAdd N j) fun h => hij ((Fin.natAdd_inj N).mp h)

/-- A word on `N` bits, shifted onto the output half of `N + N`. -/
noncomputable def natAddWord (N : ℕ) {M : ℕ} (w : GateWord N M) : GateWord (N + N) M :=
  w.map (natAddLetter N)

/-- A Pauli with its sign on `N` qubits, shifted onto the output half of `N + N`. -/
def natAddPauli (N : ℕ) (P : SignedPauli N) : SignedPauli (N + N) :=
  ⟨P.sign, ⟨Fin.append 0 P.pauli.X, Fin.append 0 P.pauli.Z⟩⟩

/-- **The identity at a precision**: the identity on `N` pairs lifted by R7 to `max 1 M`, so that a
word at precision `M ≥ 1` meets it at its own precision and no diagonal letter is left as the
identity. -/
noncomputable def idAt (N M : ℕ) : KernelSumState (N + N) :=
  liftPrecision (idState N) (max 1 M) (le_max_left 1 M)

/-- **A gate word as a presentation** `N → N`: the shifted word run on the identity at the word's
precision. -/
noncomputable def wordState (N M : ℕ) (w : GateWord N M) : KernelSumState (N + N) :=
  run (natAddWord N w) (idAt N M)

/-- **A conditioning letter as a presentation** `N → N + 1`: `conditionOutcome` of the shifted
Pauli on the identity at the protocol's precision, the outcome bit last, as in T14. -/
noncomputable def conditionState (N M : ℕ) (P : SignedPauli N) : KernelSumState (N + (N + 1)) :=
  conditionOutcome (idAt N M) (natAddPauli N P)

/-! ## The referees and the carrier properties

The amplitude theorems and the carrier theorems of the presentations above, proved at T46.3.1, in
the order of the definitions. They precede the category on classes, whose laws (T46.3.2) are read
off them: composition is the contraction by `amp_comp`, the identity is `δ_{x = y}` by
`amp_idState`. A theorem's position is outside the statement hash (tools/gate/gate.py,
`statement_hash`), and no instance's value holds `sorry` since entry 2026-10-02b, so the block
moved here at T46.3.2 with every name, type and value unchanged. -/

/-! ### Casts, scales and reindexings -/

/-- The cast keeps the carrier property. -/
theorem isCarrier_castBits {N N' : ℕ} (h : N = N') {S : KernelSumState N} (hS : IsCarrier S) :
    IsCarrier (castBits h S) := by
  subst h
  exact hS

/-- The on-support amplitude at scale `z * c` is `z` times that at scale `c`. -/
theorem ampCore_mul_scale {N m h : ℕ} (Q : DiagPhase (N + h) m) (z c : ℂ) (w : Fin N → ZMod 2) :
    ampCore m h Q (z * c) w = z * ampCore m h Q c w := by
  unfold ampCore
  ring

/-- The amplitude of a scaled presentation is `z` times the input's. -/
theorem amp_scaleBy {N : ℕ} (z : ℂ) (S : KernelSumState N) :
    amp (scaleBy z S) = fun w => z * amp S w := by
  funext w
  by_cases hw : ∃ p ∈ S.L, w = S.x₀ + p.X
  · have hw' : ∃ p ∈ (scaleBy z S).L, w = (scaleBy z S).x₀ + p.X := hw
    rw [amp_pos hw', amp_pos hw]
    exact ampCore_mul_scale S.Q z S.c w
  · have hw' : ¬ ∃ p ∈ (scaleBy z S).L, w = (scaleBy z S).x₀ + p.X := hw
    rw [amp_neg hw', amp_neg hw, mul_zero]

/-- A nonzero scale keeps the carrier property. -/
theorem isCarrier_scaleBy {N : ℕ} {z : ℂ} (hz : z ≠ 0) {S : KernelSumState N}
    (hS : IsCarrier S) : IsCarrier (scaleBy z S) := by
  refine ⟨hS.1, hS.2.1, hS.2.2.1, fun h0 => hS.2.2.2 ?_⟩
  rw [amp_scaleBy] at h0
  funext w
  have hw := congrFun h0 w
  simp only [Pi.zero_apply, mul_eq_zero] at hw
  exact hw.resolve_left hz

/-- A reindexing keeps the carrier property. -/
theorem isCarrier_reindexFreeBits {N N' : ℕ} (h : N = N') (e : Fin N ≃ Fin N')
    {S : KernelSumState N} (hS : IsCarrier S) : IsCarrier (reindexFreeBits h e S) :=
  isCarrier_castBits h (isCarrier_permuteFreeBits _ hS)

/-- A reindexing respects `StateEq`. -/
theorem reindexFreeBits_stateEq_congr {N N' : ℕ} (h : N = N') (e : Fin N ≃ Fin N')
    {S T : KernelSumState N} (hST : StateEq S T) :
    StateEq (reindexFreeBits h e S) (reindexFreeBits h e T) := by
  unfold StateEq at hST ⊢
  rw [amp_reindexFreeBits, amp_reindexFreeBits, hST]

/-! ### Two presentations appended -/

/-- The symplectic form on `N + N'` qubits is the sum of the forms on the two blocks. -/
private theorem omega_append {N N' : ℕ} (p q : Pauli (N + N')) :
    omega p q = omega (pauliLeft N N' p) (pauliLeft N N' q)
      + omega (pauliRight N N' p) (pauliRight N N' q) := by
  unfold omega
  rw [Fin.sum_univ_add, Fin.sum_univ_add]
  simp only [pauliLeft, pauliRight, LinearMap.coe_mk, AddHom.coe_mk, Function.comp_apply]
  ring

/-- **Two carrier states appended form a carrier state**: `L ⊕ L'` is Lagrangian, the precision
is the larger of two positive ones, and the amplitude is a product of two nonzero functions.
Proved at T46.3.1. -/
theorem isCarrier_appendState {N N' : ℕ} {F : KernelSumState N} {G : KernelSumState N'}
    (hF : IsCarrier F) (hG : IsCarrier G) : IsCarrier (appendState F G) := by
  refine ⟨le_trans hF.1 (le_max_left F.m G.m), ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · intro p hp q hq
    rw [omega_append, hF.2.1 _ (Submodule.mem_inf.mp hp).1 _ (Submodule.mem_inf.mp hq).1,
      hG.2.1 _ (Submodule.mem_inf.mp hp).2 _ (Submodule.mem_inf.mp hq).2, add_zero]
  · intro q hq
    rw [LinearMap.BilinForm.mem_orthogonal_iff] at hq
    refine Submodule.mem_inf.mpr ⟨hF.2.2.1 ?_, hG.2.2.1 ?_⟩
    · rw [LinearMap.BilinForm.mem_orthogonal_iff]
      intro p hp
      let r : Pauli (N + N') := ⟨Fin.append p.X 0, Fin.append p.Z 0⟩
      have hrl : pauliLeft N N' r = p := by
        apply Pauli.ext <;> exact append_comp_castAdd _ _
      have hrr : pauliRight N N' r = 0 := by
        apply Pauli.ext <;> exact append_comp_natAdd _ _
      have hr : r ∈ (appendState F G).L := by
        refine Submodule.mem_inf.mpr ⟨?_, ?_⟩
        · change pauliLeft N N' r ∈ F.L
          rw [hrl]
          exact hp
        · change pauliRight N N' r ∈ G.L
          rw [hrr]
          exact G.L.zero_mem
      have h := hq r hr
      rw [LinearMap.BilinForm.isOrtho_def, omegaBilin_apply, omega_append, hrl, hrr,
        omega_zero_left, add_zero] at h
      rw [LinearMap.BilinForm.isOrtho_def, omegaBilin_apply]
      exact h
    · rw [LinearMap.BilinForm.mem_orthogonal_iff]
      intro p hp
      let r : Pauli (N + N') := ⟨Fin.append 0 p.X, Fin.append 0 p.Z⟩
      have hrl : pauliLeft N N' r = 0 := by
        apply Pauli.ext <;> exact append_comp_castAdd _ _
      have hrr : pauliRight N N' r = p := by
        apply Pauli.ext <;> exact append_comp_natAdd _ _
      have hr : r ∈ (appendState F G).L := by
        refine Submodule.mem_inf.mpr ⟨?_, ?_⟩
        · change pauliLeft N N' r ∈ F.L
          rw [hrl]
          exact F.L.zero_mem
        · change pauliRight N N' r ∈ G.L
          rw [hrr]
          exact hp
      have h := hq r hr
      rw [LinearMap.BilinForm.isOrtho_def, omegaBilin_apply, omega_append, hrl, hrr,
        omega_zero_left, zero_add] at h
      rw [LinearMap.BilinForm.isOrtho_def, omegaBilin_apply]
      exact h
  · intro h0
    obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := Function.ne_iff.mp hF.2.2.2
    obtain ⟨v, hv⟩ := Function.ne_iff.mp hG.2.2.2
    have h := congrFun h0 (Fin.append u v)
    rw [amp_appendState] at h
    simp only [append_comp_castAdd, append_comp_natAdd, Pi.zero_apply] at h hu hv
    exact mul_ne_zero hu hv h

/-! ### The zero presentation and a carrier presentation of an amplitude -/

/-- The zero presentation has amplitude `0`. -/
theorem amp_zeroState (N : ℕ) : amp (zeroState N) = 0 :=
  amp_c_zero (zeroState N) rfl

/-- The Lagrangian `{X^v Z^u : v ∈ V, u ∈ V^⊥}` of a subspace `V` of the X-space, `V^⊥` taken for
the dot product. -/
def shadowLagrangian {N : ℕ} (V : Submodule (ZMod 2) (Fin N → ZMod 2)) :
    Submodule (ZMod 2) (Pauli N) where
  carrier := {p | p.X ∈ V ∧ ∀ v ∈ V, ∑ i, v i * p.Z i = 0}
  zero_mem' := ⟨V.zero_mem, fun v _ => by
    simp only [Z_zero, Pi.zero_apply, mul_zero, Finset.sum_const_zero]⟩
  add_mem' := fun {p q} hp hq => ⟨V.add_mem hp.1 hq.1, fun v hv => by
    simp only [Z_add, Pi.add_apply, mul_add, Finset.sum_add_distrib, hp.2 v hv, hq.2 v hv,
      add_zero]⟩
  smul_mem' := fun c p hp => ⟨V.smul_mem c hp.1, fun v hv => by
    simp only [Z_smul, Pi.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul, mul_left_comm _ c, ← Finset.mul_sum,
      hp.2 v hv, mul_zero]⟩

/-- The pure-X Paulis whose X-part lies in `V`. -/
def shadowOnly {N : ℕ} (V : Submodule (ZMod 2) (Fin N → ZMod 2)) :
    Submodule (ZMod 2) (Pauli N) where
  carrier := {p | p.X ∈ V ∧ p.Z = 0}
  zero_mem' := ⟨V.zero_mem, rfl⟩
  add_mem' := fun {p q} hp hq => ⟨V.add_mem hp.1 hq.1, by rw [Z_add, hp.2, hq.2, add_zero]⟩
  smul_mem' := fun c p hp => ⟨V.smul_mem c hp.1, by rw [Z_smul, hp.2, smul_zero]⟩

/-- The X-shadow of `shadowLagrangian V` is `V`. -/
theorem map_xProj_shadowLagrangian {N : ℕ} (V : Submodule (ZMod 2) (Fin N → ZMod 2)) :
    Submodule.map xProj (shadowLagrangian V) = V := by
  ext v
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨p, hp, rfl⟩
    rw [xProj_apply]
    exact hp.1
  · intro hv
    refine Submodule.mem_map.mpr ⟨⟨v, 0⟩, ⟨hv, fun u _ => by
      simp only [Pi.zero_apply, mul_zero, Finset.sum_const_zero]⟩, ?_⟩
    rw [xProj_apply]

/-- `shadowLagrangian V` is isotropic. -/
theorem isStabilizer_shadowLagrangian {N : ℕ}
    (V : Submodule (ZMod 2) (Fin N → ZMod 2)) : IsStabilizer (shadowLagrangian V) := by
  intro p hp q hq
  unfold omega
  have h1 : ∑ i, p.Z i * q.X i = 0 := by
    rw [← hp.2 q.X hq.1]
    exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => mul_comm _ _
  rw [h1, hq.2 p.X hp.1, add_zero]

/-- `shadowLagrangian V` is co-isotropic: a Pauli orthogonal to it has its Z-part in `V^⊥`,
tested on `X^v`, and its X-part in `V`, by the double orthogonal of `shadowOnly V`. -/
theorem orthogonal_shadowLagrangian_le {N : ℕ}
    (V : Submodule (ZMod 2) (Fin N → ZMod 2)) :
    LinearMap.BilinForm.orthogonal omegaBilin (shadowLagrangian V) ≤ shadowLagrangian V := by
  intro q hq
  rw [LinearMap.BilinForm.mem_orthogonal_iff] at hq
  have hq' : ∀ p ∈ shadowLagrangian V, omega p q = 0 := fun p hp => by
    have h := hq p hp
    rwa [LinearMap.BilinForm.isOrtho_def, omegaBilin_apply] at h
  refine ⟨?_, fun v hv => ?_⟩
  · have hmem : (⟨q.X, 0⟩ : Pauli N) ∈ shadowOnly V := by
      rw [← orthogonal_orthogonal_omegaBilin (shadowOnly V), LinearMap.BilinForm.mem_orthogonal_iff]
      intro r hr
      rw [LinearMap.BilinForm.mem_orthogonal_iff] at hr
      rw [LinearMap.BilinForm.isOrtho_def, omegaBilin_apply]
      have hz : (⟨0, r.Z⟩ : Pauli N) ∈ shadowLagrangian V := by
        refine ⟨V.zero_mem, fun v hv => ?_⟩
        have h := hr ⟨v, 0⟩ ⟨hv, rfl⟩
        rw [LinearMap.BilinForm.isOrtho_def, omegaBilin_apply] at h
        unfold omega at h
        simpa only [Pi.zero_apply, zero_mul, Finset.sum_const_zero, zero_add] using h
      have h := hq' _ hz
      unfold omega at h ⊢
      simpa only [Pi.zero_apply, mul_zero, Finset.sum_const_zero, add_zero, zero_mul] using h
    exact hmem.1
  · have h := hq' ⟨v, 0⟩ ⟨hv, fun u _ => by
      simp only [Pi.zero_apply, mul_zero, Finset.sum_const_zero]⟩
    unfold omega at h
    simpa only [Pi.zero_apply, zero_mul, Finset.sum_const_zero, zero_add] using h

-- source: papers/categorical_qm/
-- Comfort_2021_graphical_calculus_lagrangian_relations_2105.06244 definition:h7963d1a59afa
/-- **Every nonzero amplitude is a carrier state's.** `amp` reads the Lagrangian only through its
X-shadow (`amp_congr_xProj`), every subspace `V` of the X-space is the shadow of the Lagrangian
`{X^v Z^u : v ∈ V, u ∈ V^⊥}`, and the precision lifts to `1` keeping `amp` (R7, `amp_liftTo`). So
the classes of `KernelSumState N` are the classes of carrier states and the zero class, the
possibly empty relations of the corpus read on amplitudes (fidelity note, Claim 2). Proved at
T46.3.1. -/
theorem exists_carrier_of_amp_ne_zero {N : ℕ} (S : KernelSumState N) (hS : amp S ≠ 0) :
    ∃ T : KernelSumState N, IsCarrier T ∧ amp T = amp S := by
  have hamp : amp (⟨max 1 S.m, S.h, FTQCLib.Hilbert.liftTo (max 1 S.m) (le_max_right 1 S.m) S.Q,
      S.c, shadowLagrangian (Submodule.map xProj S.L), S.x₀⟩ : KernelSumState N) = amp S := by
    rw [amp_liftTo]
    exact amp_congr_xProj S.Q S.c _ S.L S.x₀ (map_xProj_shadowLagrangian _)
  refine ⟨_, ⟨le_max_left 1 S.m, isStabilizer_shadowLagrangian _,
    orthogonal_shadowLagrangian_le _, ?_⟩, hamp⟩
  rw [hamp]
  exact hS

/-- The carrier presentation of a presentation's amplitude has that amplitude. -/
theorem amp_carrierRep {N : ℕ} (S : KernelSumState N) : amp (carrierRep (amp S)) = amp S := by
  unfold carrierRep
  split_ifs with h
  · exact (Classical.choose_spec h).2
  · rw [amp_zeroState]
    by_contra hne
    exact h (exists_carrier_of_amp_ne_zero S (Ne.symm hne))

/-- The carrier presentation of a nonzero amplitude is a carrier state. -/
theorem isCarrier_carrierRep {N : ℕ} (S : KernelSumState N) (hS : amp S ≠ 0) :
    IsCarrier (carrierRep (amp S)) := by
  unfold carrierRep
  split_ifs with h
  · exact (Classical.choose_spec h).1
  · exact absurd (exists_carrier_of_amp_ne_zero S hS) h

/-! ### Contracting the shared pairs -/

/-- A sum over one bit is the value at `0` plus the value at `1`. -/
private theorem sum_zmod_two_frame (f : ZMod 2 → ℂ) : ∑ β : ZMod 2, f β = f 0 + f 1 :=
  Fin.sum_univ_two f

/-- The first half of `contractPair`, the CNOT and the conditioning of the last bit at `0`, reads
the input with the last bit set to bit `a`. -/
private theorem amp_contractPair_first {K : ℕ} (a : Fin (K + 1)) {T : KernelSumState (K + 1 + 1)}
    (hT : IsCarrier T) (v : Fin (K + 1) → ZMod 2) :
    amp (restrictZ (Fin.last (K + 1)) 0
        (run (m := T.m)
          [GateLetter.cnot (Fin.castSucc a) (Fin.last (K + 1)) (Fin.castSucc_lt_last a).ne] T)) v
      = amp T (Fin.snoc v (v a)) := by
  rw [amp_restrictZ (isCarrier_run _ hT rfl), amp_run _ hT rfl, Fin.insertNth_last']
  change amp T (DiagPhase.cnotBitMap (Fin.castSucc a) (Fin.last (K + 1)) (Fin.snoc v 0)) = _
  unfold DiagPhase.cnotBitMap
  rw [Fin.snoc_last, Fin.snoc_castSucc, zero_add, Fin.update_snoc_last]

/-- **The amplitude of one pair contracted**: on a carrier state whose contraction is nonzero, the
result is a carrier state with the referee's amplitude. The nonzero hypothesis is where the frozen
theorems ask it: `restrictZ` keeps the carrier property only where its result is nonzero, and H's
referee is stated on carrier states; each step is linear, so a zero before the end gives a zero at
the end. Proved at T46.3.1. -/
theorem amp_contractPair {K : ℕ} (a : Fin (K + 1)) {T : KernelSumState (K + 1 + 1)}
    (hT : IsCarrier T) (hne : contractPairAmp a (amp T) ≠ 0) :
    IsCarrier (contractPair a T) ∧ amp (contractPair a T) = contractPairAmp a (amp T) := by
  set S₁ := run (m := T.m)
    [GateLetter.cnot (Fin.castSucc a) (Fin.last (K + 1)) (Fin.castSucc_lt_last a).ne] T with hS₁
  have hS₁c : IsCarrier S₁ := isCarrier_run _ hT rfl
  have hS₁m : S₁.m = T.m := run_m _ T
  set S₂ := restrictZ (Fin.last (K + 1)) 0 S₁ with hS₂
  have hS₂amp : ∀ v, amp S₂ v = amp T (Fin.snoc v (v a)) := amp_contractPair_first a hT
  have hsum : ∀ w, contractPairAmp a (amp T) w = ∑ β : ZMod 2, amp S₂ (Fin.insertNth a β w) := by
    intro w
    unfold contractPairAmp
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun β _ => ?_
    rw [hS₂amp, Fin.insertNth_apply_same]
  have hS₂ne : amp S₂ ≠ 0 := by
    intro h0
    apply hne
    funext w
    rw [hsum]
    simp only [h0, Pi.zero_apply, Finset.sum_const_zero]
  have hS₂c : IsCarrier S₂ := isCarrier_restrictZ hS₁c _ _ hS₂ne
  have hS₂m : S₂.m = T.m := (restrictZ_m hS₁c.1 _ _).trans hS₁m
  set S₃ := run (m := T.m) [GateLetter.hadamard a] S₂ with hS₃
  have hS₃c : IsCarrier S₃ := isCarrier_run _ hS₂c hS₂m
  have hS₄amp : amp (restrictZ a 0 S₃) = fun w => (1 / (Real.sqrt 2 : ℂ))
      * contractPairAmp a (amp T) w := by
    funext w
    rw [amp_restrictZ hS₃c, hS₃, amp_run _ hS₂c hS₂m, hsum, sum_zmod_two_frame]
    change walshTransform a (amp S₂) (Fin.insertNth a 0 w) = _
    unfold walshTransform
    rw [Fin.update_insertNth, Fin.update_insertNth, Fin.insertNth_apply_same, signOf_zero, one_mul]
  have hsqrt : (Real.sqrt 2 : ℂ) ≠ 0 := by
    rw [Ne, Complex.ofReal_eq_zero, Real.sqrt_eq_zero (by norm_num)]
    norm_num
  have hamp : amp (contractPair a T) = contractPairAmp a (amp T) := by
    unfold contractPair
    rw [amp_scaleBy, ← hS₁, ← hS₂, ← hS₃, hS₄amp]
    funext w
    rw [← mul_assoc, mul_one_div_cancel hsqrt, one_mul]
  refine ⟨?_, hamp⟩
  have hS₄ne : amp (restrictZ a 0 S₃) ≠ 0 := by
    intro h0
    apply hne
    funext w
    have h := congrFun h0 w
    rw [hS₄amp] at h
    simp only [Pi.zero_apply, mul_eq_zero, one_div, inv_eq_zero, hsqrt, false_or] at h
    exact h
  unfold contractPair
  rw [← hS₁, ← hS₂, ← hS₃]
  exact isCarrier_scaleBy hsqrt (isCarrier_restrictZ hS₃c _ _ hS₄ne)

/-- `Fin.append` read by the value of the index. -/
private theorem append_apply_val {n k : ℕ} {α : Type*} (u : Fin n → α) (v : Fin k → α)
    (i : Fin (n + k)) :
    Fin.append u v i = if h : (i : ℕ) < n then u ⟨i, h⟩ else v ⟨i - n, by omega⟩ := by
  refine Fin.addCases (fun j => ?_) (fun j => ?_) i
  · rw [Fin.append_left, dif_pos (by simp only [Fin.val_castAdd, Fin.is_lt])]
    rfl
  · rw [Fin.append_right, dif_neg (by
      simp only [Fin.val_natAdd, add_lt_iff_neg_left, not_lt_zero, not_false_eq_true])]
    congr 1
    ext
    simp only [Fin.val_natAdd, add_tsub_cancel_left]

/-- `Fin.snoc` read by the value of the index. -/
private theorem snoc_apply_val {n : ℕ} {α : Type*} (v : Fin n → α) (x : α) (i : Fin (n + 1)) :
    (Fin.snoc v x : Fin (n + 1) → α) i = if h : (i : ℕ) < n then v ⟨i, h⟩ else x := by
  unfold Fin.snoc
  split_ifs <;> rfl

/-- `Fin.insertNth` read by the value of the index. -/
private theorem insertNth_apply_val {n : ℕ} {α : Type*} (p : Fin (n + 1)) (x : α)
    (v : Fin n → α) (i : Fin (n + 1)) :
    (Fin.insertNth p x v : Fin (n + 1) → α) i
      = if h : (i : ℕ) < p then v ⟨i, by omega⟩
        else if h' : (i : ℕ) = p then x else v ⟨i - 1, by have := i.isLt; omega⟩ := by
  rcases lt_trichotomy i p with h | h | h
  · rw [Fin.insertNth_apply_below h, dif_pos (Fin.lt_def.mp h), eq_rec_constant]
    rfl
  · subst h
    rw [Fin.insertNth_apply_same, dif_neg (lt_irrefl _), dif_pos rfl]
  · rw [Fin.insertNth_apply_above h, dif_neg (by have := Fin.lt_def.mp h; omega),
      dif_neg (by have := Fin.lt_def.mp h; omega), eq_rec_constant]
    rfl

/-- The register `contractShared` hands to `contractPair` at `m + 1` pairs: the last pair's two
bits, put back at `β`, give the register of `m + 1` pairs with that pair at `β`. -/
private theorem snoc_insertNth_append_cast {R m : ℕ} (w : Fin R → ZMod 2) (y : Fin m → ZMod 2)
    (β : ZMod 2) (h : R + ((m + 1) + (m + 1)) = R + (m + m) + 1 + 1) :
    (Fin.snoc (Fin.insertNth (⟨R + m, by omega⟩ : Fin (R + (m + m) + 1)) β
        (Fin.append w (Fin.append y y))) β : Fin (R + (m + m) + 1 + 1) → ZMod 2) ∘ Fin.cast h
      = Fin.append w (Fin.append (Fin.snoc y β : Fin (m + 1) → ZMod 2) (Fin.snoc y β)) := by
  funext i
  simp only [Function.comp_apply, append_apply_val, snoc_apply_val, insertNth_apply_val,
    Fin.val_cast]
  split_ifs <;> first
    | rfl
    | (exfalso; omega)
    | (congr 1; ext; simp only []; omega)

/-- A sum over the words of `m + 1` bits is a double sum over the first `m` bits and the last. -/
private theorem sum_snoc_split {m : ℕ} (g : (Fin (m + 1) → ZMod 2) → ℂ) :
    ∑ y', g y' = ∑ y : Fin m → ZMod 2, ∑ β : ZMod 2, g (Fin.snoc y β) := by
  rw [Finset.sum_comm, ← Fintype.sum_prod_type']
  exact (Fintype.sum_equiv (Fin.snocEquiv fun _ => ZMod 2) _ _ (fun _ => rfl)).symm

/-- Contracting the last pair, then the other `m`, is contracting all `m + 1`: the referees
agree. -/
private theorem contractSharedAmp_succ (R m : ℕ) (T : KernelSumState (R + ((m + 1) + (m + 1))))
    (h : R + ((m + 1) + (m + 1)) = R + (m + m) + 1 + 1) :
    contractSharedAmp R m (contractPairAmp (⟨R + m, by omega⟩ : Fin (R + (m + m) + 1))
        (amp (castBits h T)))
      = contractSharedAmp R (m + 1) (amp T) := by
  funext w
  unfold contractSharedAmp contractPairAmp
  rw [sum_snoc_split]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun y _ => Finset.sum_congr rfl fun β _ => ?_
  rw [amp_castBits]
  exact congrArg (amp T) (snoc_insertNth_append_cast w y β h)

/-- **The amplitude of all shared pairs contracted**: on a carrier state whose contraction is
nonzero, a carrier state with the referee's amplitude, by `amp_contractPair` pair by pair; the
sums nest by Fubini for finite sums. Proved at T46.3.1. -/
theorem amp_contractShared (R m : ℕ) {T : KernelSumState (R + (m + m))} (hT : IsCarrier T)
    (hne : contractSharedAmp R m (amp T) ≠ 0) :
    IsCarrier (contractShared R m T)
      ∧ amp (contractShared R m T) = contractSharedAmp R m (amp T) := by
  induction m with
  | zero =>
    refine ⟨hT, ?_⟩
    funext w
    unfold contractSharedAmp
    rw [Fintype.sum_unique]
    congr 1
    funext i
    rw [append_apply_val, dif_pos (by have := i.isLt; omega)]
  | succ m ih =>
    have hc : R + ((m + 1) + (m + 1)) = R + (m + m) + 1 + 1 := by omega
    have hT' : IsCarrier (castBits hc T) := isCarrier_castBits hc hT
    have hpair : contractPairAmp (⟨R + m, by omega⟩ : Fin (R + (m + m) + 1))
        (amp (castBits hc T)) ≠ 0 := by
      intro h0
      apply hne
      rw [← contractSharedAmp_succ R m T hc, h0]
      funext w
      simp only [contractSharedAmp, Pi.zero_apply, Finset.sum_const_zero]
    obtain ⟨hc', hamp'⟩ := amp_contractPair _ hT' hpair
    have hne' :
        contractSharedAmp R m (amp (contractPair ⟨R + m, by omega⟩ (castBits hc T))) ≠ 0 := by
      rw [hamp', contractSharedAmp_succ R m T hc]
      exact hne
    obtain ⟨hc'', hamp''⟩ := ih hc' hne'
    refine ⟨hc'', ?_⟩
    change amp (contractShared R m (contractPair ⟨R + m, by omega⟩ (castBits hc T))) = _
    rw [hamp'', hamp', contractSharedAmp_succ R m T hc]

/-! ### Composition on presentations -/

/-- The first factor of composition reads `(x, y)` of the register `(x, z, y, y′)`. -/
private theorem compLayout_castAdd {n m p : ℕ} (v : Fin ((n + p) + (m + m)) → ZMod 2) :
    (v ∘ compLayout n m p) ∘ Fin.castAdd (m + p)
      = Fin.append (v ∘ Fin.castAdd (m + m) ∘ Fin.castAdd p)
          (v ∘ Fin.natAdd (n + p) ∘ Fin.castAdd m) := by
  funext i
  refine Fin.addCases (fun i => ?_) (fun i => ?_) i
  · simp only [compLayout, Equiv.coe_trans, Function.comp_apply, finSumFinEquiv_symm_apply_castAdd,
      Equiv.sumCongr_apply, Sum.map_inl, Equiv.coe_refl, Equiv.sumComm_apply, id_eq,
      Equiv.sumSumSumComm_apply, Equiv.sumAssoc_symm_apply_inl, Equiv.sumAssoc_apply_inl_inl,
      finSumFinEquiv_apply_left, Fin.append_left]
  · simp only [compLayout, Equiv.coe_trans, Function.comp_apply, finSumFinEquiv_symm_apply_castAdd,
      Equiv.sumCongr_apply, Sum.map_inl, finSumFinEquiv_symm_apply_natAdd, Equiv.coe_refl,
      Equiv.sumComm_apply, id_eq, Equiv.sumSumSumComm_apply, Equiv.sumAssoc_symm_apply_inl,
      Equiv.sumAssoc_apply_inl_inr, Sum.map_inr, Sum.swap_inl, Equiv.sumAssoc_symm_apply_inr_inr,
      finSumFinEquiv_apply_left, finSumFinEquiv_apply_right, Fin.append_right]

/-- The second factor of composition reads `(y′, z)` of the register `(x, z, y, y′)`. -/
private theorem compLayout_natAdd {n m p : ℕ} (v : Fin ((n + p) + (m + m)) → ZMod 2) :
    (v ∘ compLayout n m p) ∘ Fin.natAdd (n + m)
      = Fin.append (v ∘ Fin.natAdd (n + p) ∘ Fin.natAdd m)
          (v ∘ Fin.castAdd (m + m) ∘ Fin.natAdd n) := by
  funext i
  refine Fin.addCases (fun i => ?_) (fun i => ?_) i
  · simp only [compLayout, Equiv.coe_trans, Function.comp_apply, finSumFinEquiv_symm_apply_natAdd,
      Equiv.sumCongr_apply, Sum.map_inr, finSumFinEquiv_symm_apply_castAdd, Equiv.coe_refl,
      Equiv.sumComm_apply, Sum.swap_inl, Equiv.sumSumSumComm_apply,
      Equiv.sumAssoc_symm_apply_inr_inr, id_eq, Equiv.sumAssoc_apply_inr,
      finSumFinEquiv_apply_right, Fin.natAdd_eq_addNat, Fin.append_left]
  · simp only [compLayout, Equiv.coe_trans, Function.comp_apply, finSumFinEquiv_symm_apply_natAdd,
      Equiv.sumCongr_apply, Sum.map_inr, Equiv.coe_refl, Equiv.sumComm_apply, Sum.swap_inr,
      Equiv.sumSumSumComm_apply, Equiv.sumAssoc_symm_apply_inr_inl, Sum.map_inl,
      Equiv.sumAssoc_apply_inr, Equiv.sumAssoc_apply_inl_inl, finSumFinEquiv_apply_right,
      finSumFinEquiv_apply_left, Fin.append_right]

/-- A nonzero contraction has a nonzero first factor. -/
private theorem amp_ne_zero_of_contractAmp_ne_zero_left {n m p : ℕ}
    {f : (Fin (n + m) → ZMod 2) → ℂ} {g : (Fin (m + p) → ZMod 2) → ℂ}
    (hne : contractAmp n m p f g ≠ 0) : f ≠ 0 := by
  intro h0
  apply hne
  funext w
  simp only [contractAmp, h0, Pi.zero_apply, zero_mul, Finset.sum_const_zero]

/-- A nonzero contraction has a nonzero second factor. -/
private theorem amp_ne_zero_of_contractAmp_ne_zero_right {n m p : ℕ}
    {f : (Fin (n + m) → ZMod 2) → ℂ} {g : (Fin (m + p) → ZMod 2) → ℂ}
    (hne : contractAmp n m p f g ≠ 0) : g ≠ 0 := by
  intro h0
  apply hne
  funext w
  simp only [contractAmp, h0, Pi.zero_apply, mul_zero, Finset.sum_const_zero]

/-- The referee of the shared pairs, on the appended carrier presentations read as
`(x, z, y, y′)`, is the contraction of the two amplitudes. -/
private theorem contractSharedAmp_layout {n m p : ℕ} (F : KernelSumState (n + m))
    (G : KernelSumState (m + p)) (h : (n + m) + (m + p) = (n + p) + (m + m)) :
    contractSharedAmp (n + p) m
        (amp (reindexFreeBits h (compLayout n m p)
          (appendState (carrierRep (amp F)) (carrierRep (amp G)))))
      = contractAmp n m p (amp F) (amp G) := by
  funext w
  unfold contractSharedAmp contractAmp
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun y _ => ?_
  rw [amp_reindexFreeBits, amp_appendState, amp_carrierRep, amp_carrierRep]
  change amp F ((Fin.append w (Fin.append y y) ∘ compLayout n m p) ∘ Fin.castAdd (m + p))
      * amp G ((Fin.append w (Fin.append y y) ∘ compLayout n m p) ∘ Fin.natAdd (n + m)) = _
  rw [compLayout_castAdd, compLayout_natAdd]
  congr 3
  · funext i
    simp only [Function.comp_apply, Fin.append_left]
  · funext i
    simp only [Function.comp_apply, Fin.append_right, Fin.append_left]
  · funext i
    simp only [Function.comp_apply, Fin.append_right]
  · funext i
    simp only [Function.comp_apply, Fin.append_left]

/-- Where the contraction is nonzero, the composite is a carrier state with the contraction as its
amplitude: the chain of `amp_appendState`, `amp_reindexFreeBits` and `amp_contractShared`. -/
private theorem compState_of_ne {n m p : ℕ} (F : KernelSumState (n + m))
    (G : KernelSumState (m + p)) (hne : contractAmp n m p (amp F) (amp G) ≠ 0) :
    IsCarrier (compState F G) ∧ amp (compState F G) = contractAmp n m p (amp F) (amp G) := by
  have hA := isCarrier_carrierRep F (amp_ne_zero_of_contractAmp_ne_zero_left hne)
  have hB := isCarrier_carrierRep G (amp_ne_zero_of_contractAmp_ne_zero_right hne)
  have hR := isCarrier_reindexFreeBits (show (n + m) + (m + p) = (n + p) + (m + m) by omega)
    (compLayout n m p) (isCarrier_appendState hA hB)
  have hlay := contractSharedAmp_layout F G (show (n + m) + (m + p) = (n + p) + (m + m) by omega)
  unfold compState
  rw [if_neg hne, ← hlay]
  exact amp_contractShared (n + p) m hR (hlay ▸ hne)

/-- **The composite's amplitude is the contraction**, for every pair of presentations: no shadow
test, no equal precisions, no nonzero factor. In the zero case by `amp_zeroState`; otherwise by
`amp_carrierRep`, `amp_appendState`, `amp_reindexFreeBits` and `amp_contractShared`, whose
nonzero hypothesis is the case's. Proved at T46.3.1. -/
theorem amp_comp {n m p : ℕ} (F : KernelSumState (n + m)) (G : KernelSumState (m + p)) :
    amp (compState F G) = contractAmp n m p (amp F) (amp G) := by
  by_cases h : contractAmp n m p (amp F) (amp G) = 0
  · unfold compState
    rw [if_pos h, amp_zeroState, h]
  · exact (compState_of_ne F G h).2

/-- **A nonzero composite is a carrier state.** `IsCarrier` is asked only of nonzero composites
(D10); no hypothesis on the factors is needed, since composition runs on carrier presentations.
Proved at T46.3.1. -/
theorem isCarrier_comp {n m p : ℕ} {F : KernelSumState (n + m)} {G : KernelSumState (m + p)}
    (hne : amp (compState F G) ≠ 0) : IsCarrier (compState F G) := by
  by_cases h : contractAmp n m p (amp F) (amp G) = 0
  · rw [amp_comp, h] at hne
    exact absurd rfl hne
  · exact (compState_of_ne F G h).1

/-! ### The identity and the symmetry -/

/-- A word is on the identity's support exactly when its two halves agree. -/
private theorem support_idState_iff (n : ℕ) (w : Fin (n + n) → ZMod 2) :
    (∃ p ∈ (idState n).L, w = (idState n).x₀ + p.X) ↔ w ∘ Fin.castAdd n = w ∘ Fin.natAdd n := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨p, hp, rfl⟩
    funext i
    simp only [Function.comp_apply, idState, zero_add]
    exact (hp i).1
  · intro hw
    refine ⟨⟨w, 0⟩, fun i => ⟨congrFun hw i, rfl⟩, ?_⟩
    change w = 0 + w
    rw [zero_add]

/-- On support the identity's amplitude is `1`: scale `1`, height `0`, exponent `0`. -/
private theorem ampCore_idState (n : ℕ) (w : Fin (n + n) → ZMod 2) :
    ampCore (idState n).m (idState n).h (idState n).Q (idState n).c w = 1 := by
  change ampCore 1 0 (0 : DiagPhase (n + n + 0) 1) 1 w = 1
  unfold ampCore
  simp only [pow_zero, ne_eq, one_ne_zero, not_false_eq_true, div_self, Finset.univ_unique,
    DiagPhase.realPhase, Nat.reducePow, DiagPhase.eval, Nat.add_zero, CharP.cast_eq_zero, mul_zero,
    pow_one, zero_div, Complex.ofReal_zero, Complex.exp_zero, Finset.sum_const,
    Finset.card_singleton, one_smul, mul_one]

/-- **The amplitude of the identity** is `δ_{x = y}`: `1` where the input half equals the output
half, `0` elsewhere. Proved at T46.3.1. -/
theorem amp_idState (n : ℕ) :
    amp (idState n) = fun w => if w ∘ Fin.castAdd n = w ∘ Fin.natAdd n then 1 else 0 := by
  funext w
  by_cases hw : w ∘ Fin.castAdd n = w ∘ Fin.natAdd n
  · rw [if_pos hw, amp_pos ((support_idState_iff n w).mpr hw), ampCore_idState]
  · rw [if_neg hw, amp_neg (fun h => hw ((support_idState_iff n w).mp h))]

/-- The identity's Lagrangian is isotropic: the two halves of each pair contribute equal terms. -/
private theorem isStabilizer_idL (n : ℕ) : IsStabilizer (idL n) := by
  intro p hp q hq
  unfold omega
  rw [Fin.sum_univ_add, Fin.sum_univ_add]
  have h1 : ∑ i : Fin n, p.Z (Fin.natAdd n i) * q.X (Fin.natAdd n i)
      = ∑ i : Fin n, p.Z (Fin.castAdd n i) * q.X (Fin.castAdd n i) :=
    Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => by rw [(hp i).2, (hq i).1]
  have h2 : ∑ i : Fin n, p.X (Fin.natAdd n i) * q.Z (Fin.natAdd n i)
      = ∑ i : Fin n, p.X (Fin.castAdd n i) * q.Z (Fin.castAdd n i) :=
    Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => by rw [(hp i).1, (hq i).2]
  rw [h1, h2, CharTwo.add_self_eq_zero, CharTwo.add_self_eq_zero, add_zero]

/-- The identity's Lagrangian is co-isotropic: tested on `X_iX_{n+i}` and `Z_iZ_{n+i}`. -/
private theorem orthogonal_idL_le (n : ℕ) :
    LinearMap.BilinForm.orthogonal omegaBilin (idL n) ≤ idL n := by
  intro q hq
  rw [LinearMap.BilinForm.mem_orthogonal_iff] at hq
  have hq' : ∀ p ∈ idL n, omega p q = 0 := fun p hp => by
    have h := hq p hp
    rwa [LinearMap.BilinForm.isOrtho_def, omegaBilin_apply] at h
  have hpair : ∀ i : Fin n, ∀ f : Fin (n + n) → ZMod 2,
      ∑ k, (Pi.single (Fin.castAdd n i) 1 + Pi.single (Fin.natAdd n i) 1 : Fin (n + n) → ZMod 2) k
          * f k = f (Fin.castAdd n i) + f (Fin.natAdd n i) := by
    intro i f
    simp only [Pi.add_apply, add_mul, Finset.sum_add_distrib, Pi.single_apply, ite_mul, one_mul,
      zero_mul, Finset.sum_ite_eq', Finset.mem_univ, if_true]
  have hmem : ∀ i : Fin n, ∀ j : Fin n,
      (Pi.single (Fin.castAdd n i) 1 + Pi.single (Fin.natAdd n i) 1 : Fin (n + n) → ZMod 2)
          (Fin.castAdd n j)
        = (Pi.single (Fin.castAdd n i) 1 + Pi.single (Fin.natAdd n i) 1 : Fin (n + n) → ZMod 2)
          (Fin.natAdd n j) := by
    intro i j
    have h1 : Fin.castAdd n j ≠ Fin.natAdd n i := castAdd_ne_natAdd j i
    have h2 : Fin.natAdd n j ≠ Fin.castAdd n i := fun h => castAdd_ne_natAdd i j h.symm
    simp only [Pi.add_apply, Pi.single_apply, h1, h2, if_false, add_zero, zero_add,
      (Fin.castAdd_injective n n).eq_iff, (Fin.natAdd_injective n n).eq_iff]
  have hsame : ∀ a b : ZMod 2, a + b = 0 → a = b := by decide
  intro i
  constructor
  · have h := hq' ⟨0, Pi.single (Fin.castAdd n i) 1 + Pi.single (Fin.natAdd n i) 1⟩
      (fun j => ⟨rfl, hmem i j⟩)
    unfold omega at h
    simp only [Pi.zero_apply, zero_mul, Finset.sum_const_zero, add_zero] at h
    rw [hpair] at h
    exact hsame _ _ h
  · have h := hq' ⟨Pi.single (Fin.castAdd n i) 1 + Pi.single (Fin.natAdd n i) 1, 0⟩
      (fun j => ⟨hmem i j, rfl⟩)
    unfold omega at h
    simp only [Pi.zero_apply, zero_mul, Finset.sum_const_zero, zero_add] at h
    rw [hpair] at h
    exact hsame _ _ h

/-- The identity is a carrier state: the Bell floor of `n` pairs, at precision `1` and scale `1`. Public for T49,
whose Choi state is built on it (docs/STEPS.md, entry 2026-10-02h). -/
theorem isCarrier_idState (n : ℕ) : IsCarrier (idState n) := by
  refine ⟨le_refl 1, isStabilizer_idL n, orthogonal_idL_le n, fun h0 => ?_⟩
  have h := congrFun h0 0
  rw [amp_idState] at h
  simp only [Pi.zero_apply] at h
  rw [if_pos (by funext i; rfl)] at h
  exact one_ne_zero h

/-- **The amplitude of the symmetry**: `1` where the input `(x₁, x₂)` equals the output read as
`(y₁, y₂)` with `y₂` the first `m` output bits and `y₁` the last `n`, `0` elsewhere. Proved at
T46.3.1. -/
theorem amp_swapState (n m : ℕ) :
    amp (swapState n m) = fun w =>
      if w ∘ Fin.castAdd (m + n)
          = Fin.append (w ∘ Fin.natAdd (n + m) ∘ Fin.natAdd m)
              (w ∘ Fin.natAdd (n + m) ∘ Fin.castAdd n)
        then 1 else 0 := by
  funext w
  unfold swapState
  rw [amp_reindexFreeBits, amp_idState]
  have hl : (w ∘ (finSumFinEquiv.symm.trans ((Equiv.sumCongr (Equiv.refl (Fin (n + m)))
      finAddFlip).trans finSumFinEquiv))) ∘ Fin.castAdd (n + m) = w ∘ Fin.castAdd (m + n) := by
    funext i
    simp only [Function.comp_apply, Equiv.coe_trans, finSumFinEquiv_symm_apply_castAdd,
      Equiv.sumCongr_apply, Sum.map_inl, Equiv.coe_refl, id_eq, finSumFinEquiv_apply_left]
  have hr : (w ∘ (finSumFinEquiv.symm.trans ((Equiv.sumCongr (Equiv.refl (Fin (n + m)))
      finAddFlip).trans finSumFinEquiv))) ∘ Fin.natAdd (n + m)
        = Fin.append (w ∘ Fin.natAdd (n + m) ∘ Fin.natAdd m)
            (w ∘ Fin.natAdd (n + m) ∘ Fin.castAdd n) := by
    funext i
    refine Fin.addCases (fun i => ?_) (fun i => ?_) i
    · simp only [Function.comp_apply, Equiv.coe_trans, finSumFinEquiv_symm_apply_natAdd,
        Equiv.sumCongr_apply, Sum.map_inr, finAddFlip_apply_castAdd, finSumFinEquiv_apply_right,
        Fin.append_left]
    · simp only [Function.comp_apply, Equiv.coe_trans, finSumFinEquiv_symm_apply_natAdd,
        Equiv.sumCongr_apply, Sum.map_inr, finAddFlip_apply_natAdd, finSumFinEquiv_apply_right,
        Fin.append_right]
  simp only []
  rw [hl, hr]

/-! ### The letters -/

/-- The point mass at `x`. -/
noncomputable def delta {N : ℕ} (x : Fin N → ZMod 2) : (Fin N → ZMod 2) → ℂ :=
  fun u => if u = x then 1 else 0

/-- The identity's amplitude at `(x, u)` is the point mass at `x`, read at `u`. -/
private theorem amp_idState_append (N : ℕ) (x u : Fin N → ZMod 2) :
    amp (idState N) (Fin.append x u) = delta x u := by
  rw [amp_idState]
  simp only [append_comp_castAdd, append_comp_natAdd]
  unfold delta
  by_cases h : u = x
  · rw [if_pos h.symm, if_pos h]
  · rw [if_neg (fun h' => h h'.symm), if_neg h]

/-- The identity at a precision is a carrier state. -/
private theorem isCarrier_idAt (N M : ℕ) : IsCarrier (idAt N M) :=
  isCarrier_liftPrecision (isCarrier_idState N) _ _

/-- The identity at a precision has the identity's amplitude. -/
private theorem amp_idAt (N M : ℕ) : amp (idAt N M) = amp (idState N) :=
  amp_liftPrecision _ _ _

/-- A shifted letter acts on the output half alone: its referee at `(x, u)` is the letter's on the
slice at `x`. -/
private theorem letterAmp_natAddLetter (N : ℕ) {M : ℕ} (l : GateLetter N M)
    (F : (Fin (N + N) → ZMod 2) → ℂ) (x : Fin N → ZMod 2) :
    (fun u => letterAmp (natAddLetter N l) F (Fin.append x u))
      = letterAmp l (fun u => F (Fin.append x u)) := by
  funext u
  cases l with
  | hadamard k =>
    change walshTransform (Fin.natAdd N k) F (Fin.append x u)
      = walshTransform k (fun u => F (Fin.append x u)) u
    unfold walshTransform
    rw [update_append_natAdd, update_append_natAdd, Fin.append_right]
  | diagonal D =>
    change charOf M (DiagPhase.eval (MvPolynomial.rename (Fin.natAdd N) D) (Fin.append x u))
        * F (Fin.append x u) = charOf M (DiagPhase.eval D u) * F (Fin.append x u)
    rw [DiagPhase.eval_rename, append_comp_natAdd]
  | cnot i j hij =>
    change F (DiagPhase.cnotBitMap (Fin.natAdd N i) (Fin.natAdd N j) (Fin.append x u))
      = F (Fin.append x (DiagPhase.cnotBitMap i j u))
    unfold DiagPhase.cnotBitMap
    rw [Fin.append_right, Fin.append_right, update_append_natAdd]

/-- A shifted word acts on the output half alone, letter by letter. -/
private theorem runAmp_natAddWord (N : ℕ) {M : ℕ} (w : GateWord N M)
    (F : (Fin (N + N) → ZMod 2) → ℂ) (x y : Fin N → ZMod 2) :
    runAmp (natAddWord N w) F (Fin.append x y) = runAmp w (fun u => F (Fin.append x u)) y := by
  induction w generalizing F with
  | nil => rfl
  | cons l w ih =>
    change runAmp (natAddWord N w) (letterAmp (natAddLetter N l) F) (Fin.append x y) = _
    rw [ih, letterAmp_natAddLetter, runAmp_cons]

/-- **The amplitude of a word's presentation** at `(x, y)` is the word's referee on the point mass
at `x`, read at `y`: the input bits are spectators of every shifted letter. `1 ≤ M` is what
`amp_run` needs of the identity's lifted precision. Proved at T46.3.1. -/
theorem amp_wordState (N M : ℕ) (w : GateWord N M) (hM : 1 ≤ M) (x y : Fin N → ZMod 2) :
    amp (wordState N M w) (Fin.append x y) = runAmp w (delta x) y := by
  unfold wordState
  rw [amp_run _ (isCarrier_idAt N M) (max_eq_right hM), amp_idAt, runAmp_natAddWord]
  congr 1
  funext u
  exact amp_idState_append N x u

/-- The Z-dot of a Pauli shifted onto the output half reads the output half alone. -/
private theorem zDot_natAddPauli (N : ℕ) (p : Pauli N) (x u : Fin N → ZMod 2) :
    zDot (⟨Fin.append 0 p.X, Fin.append 0 p.Z⟩ : Pauli (N + N)) (Fin.append x u) = zDot p u := by
  unfold zDot
  rw [Fin.sum_univ_add]
  simp only [Fin.append_left, Fin.append_right, Pi.zero_apply, ZMod.val_zero, zero_mul,
    Finset.sum_const_zero, zero_add]

/-- Adding a word supported on the output half adds it to the output half. -/
private theorem append_add_append_zero (N : ℕ) (x y v : Fin N → ZMod 2) :
    Fin.append x y + Fin.append 0 v = Fin.append x (y + v) := by
  funext i
  refine Fin.addCases (fun i => ?_) (fun i => ?_) i
  · simp only [Pi.add_apply, Fin.append_left, Pi.zero_apply, add_zero]
  · simp only [Pi.add_apply, Fin.append_right]

/-- **The amplitude of a conditioning letter's presentation** at `(x, (y, b))` is the projection
`Π_b` of the point mass at `x`, read at `y` (`amp_conditionOutcome`, the identity's Lagrangian
being co-isotropic). Proved at T46.3.1. -/
theorem amp_conditionState (N M : ℕ) (P : SignedPauli N) (x y : Fin N → ZMod 2) (b : ZMod 2) :
    amp (conditionState N M P) (Fin.append x (Fin.snoc y b : Fin (N + 1) → ZMod 2))
      = pauliProjection P b (delta x) y := by
  unfold conditionState
  rw [Fin.append_snoc, amp_conditionOutcome _ (orthogonal_idL_le N)]
  simp only [Fin.snoc_last, Fin.init_snoc]
  rw [pauliProjection_apply, pauliProjection_apply, amp_idAt]
  have hX : (natAddPauli N P).pauli.X = Fin.append 0 P.pauli.X := rfl
  rw [hX, append_add_append_zero, amp_idState_append, amp_idState_append]
  unfold shiftFactor
  have hY : yWeight (natAddPauli N P).pauli = yWeight P.pauli := by
    unfold yWeight
    rw [hX]
    exact zDot_natAddPauli N P.pauli 0 P.pauli.X
  rw [hY, hX, append_add_append_zero]
  rw [show zDot (natAddPauli N P).pauli (Fin.append x (y + P.pauli.X))
      = zDot P.pauli (y + P.pauli.X) from zDot_natAddPauli N P.pauli x _]
  rfl

/-! ## The category on classes -/

namespace FrameCategory

-- source: papers/categorical_qm/
-- Comfort_2021_graphical_calculus_lagrangian_relations_2105.06244 definition:h995b6231ad87
/-- **An object**: a register size. A type wrapping `ℕ`, not `ℕ` itself, since Mathlib's
`Preorder.smallCategory` already makes `ℕ` a category, the order (LN.6); the corpus's props have
the natural numbers as objects. -/
structure Obj where
  /-- The number of bits. -/
  bits : ℕ

/-- The tensor of objects: the registers side by side. -/
def tensorObj (a b : Obj) : Obj := ⟨a.bits + b.bits⟩

-- source: papers/categorical_qm/
-- Comfort_2021_graphical_calculus_lagrangian_relations_2105.06244 definition:h7963d1a59afa
/-- **A morphism** `a → b`: a `StateEq` class of `KernelSumState (a.bits + b.bits)`, the quotient by
`stateSetoid`, the zero class included; the corpus's possibly empty relations between the two
sides, read on amplitudes. Never a chosen presentation. -/
noncomputable def Hom (a b : Obj) : Type := Quotient (stateSetoid (a.bits + b.bits))

/-- The class of a presentation. -/
noncomputable def toHom {a b : Obj} (F : KernelSumState (a.bits + b.bits)) : Hom a b :=
  Quotient.mk (stateSetoid (a.bits + b.bits)) F

/-- Two presentations give one morphism exactly when they are `StateEq`. -/
theorem toHom_eq_toHom_iff {a b : Obj} (F G : KernelSumState (a.bits + b.bits)) :
    toHom F = toHom G ↔ StateEq F G :=
  Quotient.eq

/-- **Composition**, diagrammatic: `comp f g` is `f` then `g`, the class of `compState` on any
presentations (`comp_stateEq_congr`). -/
noncomputable def comp {a b c : Obj} (f : Hom a b) (g : Hom b c) : Hom a c :=
  Quotient.lift₂ (fun F G => (toHom (compState F G) : Hom a c))
    (fun _ _ _ _ hF hG => Quotient.sound (comp_stateEq_congr hF hG)) f g

/-- **The identity**: the class of `idState`. -/
noncomputable def id (a : Obj) : Hom a a := toHom (idState a.bits)

/-- **The zero morphism**: the class of the zero presentation. -/
noncomputable def zero (a b : Obj) : Hom a b := toHom (zeroState (a.bits + b.bits))

/-- **The tensor**: the class of `tensorState` on any presentations (`tensor_stateEq_congr`). -/
noncomputable def tensor {a b a' b' : Obj} (f : Hom a b) (g : Hom a' b') :
    Hom (tensorObj a a') (tensorObj b b') :=
  Quotient.lift₂ (fun F G => (toHom (tensorState F G) : Hom (tensorObj a a') (tensorObj b b')))
    (fun _ _ _ _ hF hG => Quotient.sound (tensor_stateEq_congr hF hG)) f g

/-- **The symmetry**: the class of `swapState`. -/
noncomputable def swap (a b : Obj) : Hom (tensorObj a b) (tensorObj b a) :=
  toHom (swapState a.bits b.bits)

/-- **A cast of a morphism** between objects of equal sizes: the class reindexed by `castBits`,
which keeps `amp`. The associator `(a ⊗ b) ⊗ c → a ⊗ (b ⊗ c)` and the unitors `0 ⊗ a → a` and
`a ⊗ 0 → a` are casts of identities, since the objects add strictly (`Nat.add_assoc`,
`Nat.zero_add`, `Nat.add_zero`). -/
noncomputable def castHom {a b a' b' : Obj} (ha : a.bits = a'.bits) (hb : b.bits = b'.bits)
    (f : Hom a b) : Hom a' b' :=
  Quotient.map (castBits (by rw [ha, hb])) (fun _ _ hF => castBits_stateEq_congr _ hF) f

/-- The composite of a presentation's class with another's is the class of their composite. -/
theorem comp_toHom {a b c : Obj} (F : KernelSumState (a.bits + b.bits))
    (G : KernelSumState (b.bits + c.bits)) : comp (toHom F) (toHom G) = toHom (compState F G) :=
  rfl

/-- The tensor of two presentations' classes is the class of their tensor. -/
theorem tensor_toHom {a b a' b' : Obj} (F : KernelSumState (a.bits + b.bits))
    (G : KernelSumState (a'.bits + b'.bits)) :
    tensor (toHom F) (toHom G) = toHom (tensorState F G) :=
  rfl

/-! ### The entries of a morphism

A class is its amplitude, read as a matrix: `entry f x y` is `f(x, y)`. Every law below is proved
on entries (`hom_ext`). -/

/-- The entry of a morphism at input `x` and output `y`: its amplitude at `(x, y)`. -/
private noncomputable def entry {a b : Obj} (f : Hom a b) (x : Fin a.bits → ZMod 2)
    (y : Fin b.bits → ZMod 2) : ℂ :=
  Quotient.lift (fun F : KernelSumState (a.bits + b.bits) => amp F (Fin.append x y))
    (fun _ _ hFG => congrFun (hFG : amp _ = amp _) _) f

/-- The entry of a presentation's class is the presentation's amplitude. -/
private theorem entry_toHom {a b : Obj} (F : KernelSumState (a.bits + b.bits))
    (x : Fin a.bits → ZMod 2) (y : Fin b.bits → ZMod 2) :
    entry (toHom F) x y = amp F (Fin.append x y) :=
  rfl

private theorem exists_toHom {a b : Obj} (f : Hom a b) : ∃ F, toHom F = f :=
  Quotient.exists_rep f

/-- Two morphisms with the same entries are equal. -/
private theorem hom_ext {a b : Obj} {f g : Hom a b} (h : ∀ x y, entry f x y = entry g x y) :
    f = g := by
  obtain ⟨F, rfl⟩ := exists_toHom f
  obtain ⟨G, rfl⟩ := exists_toHom g
  refine (toHom_eq_toHom_iff F G).mpr (funext fun w => ?_)
  have hw := h (fun i => w (Fin.castAdd b.bits i)) (fun i => w (Fin.natAdd a.bits i))
  rwa [entry_toHom, entry_toHom, Fin.append_castAdd_natAdd] at hw

/-! ## The laws, proved on entries

Every law is an identity of amplitudes, so each is proved on entries (`hom_ext`): composition is the
contraction (`entry_comp`, from `amp_comp`), the identity is `δ_{x = y}` (`entry_id`), the tensor
multiplies the two factors' entries (`entry_tensor`), and a cast reads the words through `Fin.cast`
(`entry_castHom`). The identity, the symmetry, the casts of identities, and the tensors and
composites of these move bits (`IsPermBy`), so the hexagons, the pentagon, the triangle and the
inverse laws of the associator and the unitors are equalities of index maps, checked on values.

The laws on classes (`comp_assoc`, `id_comp`, `comp_id`, `tensor_comp`, `tensor_id`, `swap_swap`,
`swap_natural`, `swap_hexagon`, `tensor_assoc`, `tensor_id_left`, `tensor_id_right`) are stated
and proved here, after the referees they read; the Mathlib instances follow them. -/

/-! ### Composition, the identity, the tensor and the casts on entries -/

private theorem entry_comp {a b c : Obj} (f : Hom a b) (g : Hom b c) (x : Fin a.bits → ZMod 2)
    (z : Fin c.bits → ZMod 2) : entry (comp f g) x z = ∑ y, entry f x y * entry g y z := by
  obtain ⟨F, rfl⟩ := exists_toHom f
  obtain ⟨G, rfl⟩ := exists_toHom g
  rw [comp_toHom, entry_toHom, amp_comp]
  unfold contractAmp
  simp only [append_comp_castAdd, append_comp_natAdd, entry_toHom]

private theorem entry_id (a : Obj) (x y : Fin a.bits → ZMod 2) :
    entry (id a) x y = if y = x then 1 else 0 := by
  change amp (idState a.bits) (Fin.append x y) = _
  rw [amp_idState]
  simp only [append_comp_castAdd, append_comp_natAdd, eq_comm]

private theorem entry_tensor {a b a' b' : Obj} (f : Hom a b) (g : Hom a' b')
    (u : Fin (a.bits + a'.bits) → ZMod 2) (v : Fin (b.bits + b'.bits) → ZMod 2) :
    entry (tensor f g) u v
      = entry f (u ∘ Fin.castAdd a'.bits) (v ∘ Fin.castAdd b'.bits)
        * entry g (u ∘ Fin.natAdd a.bits) (v ∘ Fin.natAdd b.bits) := by
  obtain ⟨F, rfl⟩ := exists_toHom f
  obtain ⟨G, rfl⟩ := exists_toHom g
  change amp (tensorState F G) (Fin.append u v) = amp F _ * amp G _
  rw [amp_tensorState]
  simp only [← Function.comp_assoc, append_comp_castAdd, append_comp_natAdd]

/-- A cast of an appended word is the cast halves appended. -/
private theorem append_comp_cast {n m n' m' : ℕ} {α : Type*} (ha : n = n') (hb : m = m')
    (h : n + m = n' + m') (x : Fin n' → α) (y : Fin m' → α) :
    Fin.append x y ∘ Fin.cast h = Fin.append (x ∘ Fin.cast ha) (y ∘ Fin.cast hb) := by
  subst ha
  subst hb
  simp only [Fin.cast_refl, Function.comp_id]

private theorem entry_castHom {a b a' b' : Obj} (ha : a.bits = a'.bits) (hb : b.bits = b'.bits)
    (f : Hom a b) (x : Fin a'.bits → ZMod 2) (y : Fin b'.bits → ZMod 2) :
    entry (castHom ha hb f) x y = entry f (x ∘ Fin.cast ha) (y ∘ Fin.cast hb) := by
  obtain ⟨F, rfl⟩ := exists_toHom f
  change amp (castBits _ F) (Fin.append x y) = amp F (Fin.append _ _)
  rw [amp_castBits]
  exact congrArg (amp F) (append_comp_cast ha hb _ x y)

/-- A word is its two blocks. -/
private theorem word_ext {n n' : ℕ} {α : Type*} {u v : Fin (n + n') → α}
    (h₁ : u ∘ Fin.castAdd n' = v ∘ Fin.castAdd n') (h₂ : u ∘ Fin.natAdd n = v ∘ Fin.natAdd n) :
    u = v := by
  funext i
  exact Fin.addCases (fun i => congrFun h₁ i) (fun i => congrFun h₂ i) i

/-- Entries at equal words are equal. -/
private theorem entry_congr {a b : Obj} {f : Hom a b} {x x' : Fin a.bits → ZMod 2}
    {y y' : Fin b.bits → ZMod 2} (hx : x = x') (hy : y = y') : entry f x y = entry f x' y' := by
  rw [hx, hy]

/-- Two readings of a word agree when the index maps agree on values. -/
private theorem comp_eq_comp_of_val {n k : ℕ} {α : Type*} (x : Fin n → α) {ρ ρ' : Fin k → Fin n}
    (h : ∀ j, (ρ j : ℕ) = ρ' j) : x ∘ ρ = x ∘ ρ' := by
  funext j
  exact congrArg x (Fin.ext (h j))

/-- `Fin.append` of two index maps, read by value. -/
private theorem val_append_index {m n k : ℕ} (f : Fin m → Fin k) (g : Fin n → Fin k)
    (i : Fin (m + n)) :
    ((Fin.append f g i : Fin k) : ℕ)
      = if h : (i : ℕ) < m then (f ⟨i, h⟩ : ℕ) else (g ⟨i - m, by omega⟩ : ℕ) := by
  refine Fin.addCases (fun j => ?_) (fun j => ?_) i
  · rw [Fin.append_left, dif_pos (by simp only [Fin.val_castAdd, Fin.is_lt])]
    rfl
  · rw [Fin.append_right, dif_neg (by simp only [Fin.val_natAdd]; omega)]
    congr 2
    ext
    simp only [Fin.val_natAdd, add_tsub_cancel_left]

/-- An equation `u = v ∘ σ` solved for `v`, when `τ` inverts `σ`. -/
private theorem eq_comp_iff {n m : ℕ} {α : Type*} {u : Fin n → α} {v : Fin m → α}
    {σ : Fin n → Fin m} {τ : Fin m → Fin n} (h₁ : ∀ i, τ (σ i) = i) (h₂ : ∀ j, σ (τ j) = j) :
    u = v ∘ σ ↔ v = u ∘ τ := by
  constructor
  · rintro rfl
    funext j
    simp only [Function.comp_apply, h₂]
  · rintro rfl
    funext i
    simp only [Function.comp_apply, h₁]

/-! ### The laws on general morphisms -/

/-- **Associativity**, up to `StateEq`: that of the contraction, a finite sum. Proved at T46.3.2. -/
theorem comp_assoc {a b c d : Obj} (f : Hom a b) (g : Hom b c) (h : Hom c d) :
    comp (comp f g) h = comp f (comp g h) := by
  refine hom_ext fun x w => ?_
  simp only [entry_comp, Finset.sum_mul, Finset.mul_sum, mul_assoc]
  exact Finset.sum_comm

/-- **The left unit law**: `δ_{x = y}` at scale `1` is a left unit for the contraction. Proved at
T46.3.2. -/
theorem id_comp {a b : Obj} (f : Hom a b) : comp (id a) f = f := by
  refine hom_ext fun x z => ?_
  simp only [entry_comp, entry_id, ite_mul, one_mul, zero_mul, Finset.sum_ite_eq',
    Finset.mem_univ, if_true]

/-- **The right unit law**: `δ_{x = y}` at scale `1` is a right unit for the contraction. Proved at
T46.3.2. -/
theorem comp_id {a b : Obj} (f : Hom a b) : comp f (id b) = f := by
  refine hom_ext fun x z => ?_
  simp only [entry_comp, entry_id, mul_ite, mul_one, mul_zero, Finset.sum_ite_eq,
    Finset.mem_univ, if_true]

/-- **The interchange law**: the tensor of two composites is the composite of the tensors, since
the sums over the two shared registers factor. Proved at T46.3.2. -/
theorem tensor_comp {a b c a' b' c' : Obj} (f : Hom a b) (g : Hom b c) (f' : Hom a' b')
    (g' : Hom b' c') : tensor (comp f g) (comp f' g') = comp (tensor f f') (tensor g g') := by
  refine hom_ext fun u w => ?_
  rw [entry_tensor, entry_comp, entry_comp, entry_comp, Finset.sum_mul_sum]
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (sum_append_split (h := b.bits) (h' := b'.bits) _).symm
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun y _ => Finset.sum_congr rfl fun y' _ => ?_
  rw [entry_tensor, entry_tensor, append_comp_castAdd, append_comp_natAdd]
  ring

/-- **The tensor of identities is the identity**, which the middle swap makes true and the bare
`Fin.append` breaks (framing note, case I2). Proved at T46.3.2. -/
theorem tensor_id (a a' : Obj) : tensor (id a) (id a') = id (tensorObj a a') := by
  refine hom_ext fun u v => ?_
  rw [entry_tensor, entry_id, entry_id, entry_id, ite_zero_mul_ite_zero, mul_one]
  refine if_congr ⟨fun h => word_ext h.1 h.2, fun h => ⟨?_, ?_⟩⟩ rfl rfl
  · rw [h]
  · rw [h]

/-! ### Permutation morphisms -/

/-- `P` moves bits: its entry at `(x, y)` is `1` when the output `y` is the input read through the
index map `τ`, and `0` elsewhere. -/
private def IsPermBy {a b : Obj} (P : Hom a b) (τ : Fin b.bits → Fin a.bits) : Prop :=
  ∀ x y, entry P x y = if y = x ∘ τ then 1 else 0

/-- Two permutation morphisms with index maps equal on values are equal. -/
private theorem perm_eq {a b : Obj} {P Q : Hom a b} {τ ρ : Fin b.bits → Fin a.bits}
    (hP : IsPermBy P τ) (hQ : IsPermBy Q ρ) (h : ∀ j, (τ j : ℕ) = ρ j) : P = Q := by
  refine hom_ext fun x y => ?_
  rw [hP, hQ, comp_eq_comp_of_val x h]

private theorem isPermBy_id (a : Obj) : IsPermBy (id a) (fun j => j) := by
  intro x y
  rw [entry_id]
  rfl

/-- The index map of the symmetry `a ⊗ b → b ⊗ a`: output bit `j < b` is input bit `a + j`. -/
private def swapIndex (a b : ℕ) : Fin (b + a) → Fin (a + b) :=
  Fin.append (fun j : Fin b => Fin.natAdd a j) (fun j : Fin a => Fin.castAdd b j)

private theorem val_swapIndex (a b : ℕ) (j : Fin (b + a)) :
    (swapIndex a b j : ℕ) = if (j : ℕ) < b then a + j else j - b := by
  unfold swapIndex
  rw [val_append_index]
  split_ifs <;> simp only [Fin.val_natAdd, Fin.val_castAdd]

private theorem swapIndex_swapIndex (a b : ℕ) (j : Fin (b + a)) :
    swapIndex b a (swapIndex a b j) = j := by
  ext
  rw [val_swapIndex, val_swapIndex]
  split_ifs <;> omega

/-- The symmetry's amplitude at `(u, v)`: `1` when `v` is `u` read through `swapIndex`. -/
private theorem amp_swapState_append (n m : ℕ) (u : Fin (n + m) → ZMod 2)
    (v : Fin (m + n) → ZMod 2) :
    amp (swapState n m) (Fin.append u v) = if v = u ∘ swapIndex n m then 1 else 0 := by
  rw [amp_swapState]
  simp only [append_comp_castAdd, ← Function.comp_assoc, append_comp_natAdd]
  refine if_congr ?_ rfl rfl
  have hσ : Fin.append (v ∘ Fin.natAdd m) (v ∘ Fin.castAdd n) = v ∘ swapIndex m n := by
    funext i
    refine Fin.addCases (fun i => ?_) (fun i => ?_) i
    · simp only [swapIndex, Function.comp_apply, Fin.append_left]
    · simp only [swapIndex, Function.comp_apply, Fin.append_right]
  rw [hσ]
  exact eq_comp_iff (swapIndex_swapIndex _ _) (swapIndex_swapIndex _ _)

private theorem isPermBy_swap (a b : Obj) : IsPermBy (swap a b) (swapIndex a.bits b.bits) :=
  fun u v => amp_swapState_append a.bits b.bits u v

private theorem isPermBy_comp {a b c : Obj} {P : Hom a b} {Q : Hom b c}
    {τ : Fin b.bits → Fin a.bits} {ρ : Fin c.bits → Fin b.bits} (hP : IsPermBy P τ)
    (hQ : IsPermBy Q ρ) : IsPermBy (comp P Q) (fun j => τ (ρ j)) := by
  intro x z
  unfold IsPermBy at hP hQ
  simp only [entry_comp, hP, hQ, ite_mul, one_mul, zero_mul, Finset.sum_ite_eq',
    Finset.mem_univ, if_true]
  rfl

private theorem isPermBy_tensor {a b a' b' : Obj} {P : Hom a b} {Q : Hom a' b'}
    {τ : Fin b.bits → Fin a.bits} {ρ : Fin b'.bits → Fin a'.bits} (hP : IsPermBy P τ)
    (hQ : IsPermBy Q ρ) :
    IsPermBy (tensor P Q)
      (Fin.append (fun j => Fin.castAdd a'.bits (τ j)) (fun j => Fin.natAdd a.bits (ρ j))) := by
  intro u v
  rw [entry_tensor, hP, hQ, ite_zero_mul_ite_zero, mul_one]
  have h₁ : (u ∘ Fin.append (fun j => Fin.castAdd a'.bits (τ j))
      (fun j => Fin.natAdd a.bits (ρ j))) ∘ Fin.castAdd b'.bits
        = (u ∘ Fin.castAdd a'.bits) ∘ τ := by
    funext j
    simp only [Function.comp_apply, Fin.append_left]
  have h₂ : (u ∘ Fin.append (fun j => Fin.castAdd a'.bits (τ j))
      (fun j => Fin.natAdd a.bits (ρ j))) ∘ Fin.natAdd b.bits = (u ∘ Fin.natAdd a.bits) ∘ ρ := by
    funext j
    simp only [Function.comp_apply, Fin.append_right]
  refine if_congr ⟨fun h => word_ext (h.1.trans h₁.symm) (h.2.trans h₂.symm), fun h => ?_⟩ rfl rfl
  rw [h]
  exact ⟨h₁, h₂⟩

private theorem isPermBy_castHom {a b a' b' : Obj} (ha : a.bits = a'.bits) (hb : b.bits = b'.bits)
    {P : Hom a b} {τ : Fin b.bits → Fin a.bits} (hP : IsPermBy P τ) :
    IsPermBy (castHom ha hb P) (fun j => Fin.cast ha (τ (Fin.cast hb.symm j))) := by
  intro x y
  rw [entry_castHom, hP]
  refine if_congr ?_ rfl rfl
  constructor
  · intro h
    funext j
    have := congrFun h (Fin.cast hb.symm j)
    simp only [Function.comp_apply, Fin.cast_cast, Fin.cast_eq_self] at this ⊢
    exact this
  · rintro rfl
    funext j
    simp only [Function.comp_apply, Fin.cast_cast, Fin.cast_eq_self]

/-- Composing on the left with a permutation morphism reads the input through its index map. -/
private theorem entry_comp_perm_left {a b c : Obj} {P : Hom a b} {τ : Fin b.bits → Fin a.bits}
    (hP : IsPermBy P τ) (g : Hom b c) (x : Fin a.bits → ZMod 2) (z : Fin c.bits → ZMod 2) :
    entry (comp P g) x z = entry g (x ∘ τ) z := by
  unfold IsPermBy at hP
  simp only [entry_comp, hP, ite_mul, one_mul, zero_mul, Finset.sum_ite_eq', Finset.mem_univ,
    if_true]

/-- Composing on the right with a permutation morphism reads the output through the inverse of
its index map. -/
private theorem entry_comp_perm_right {a b c : Obj} {P : Hom b c} {τ : Fin c.bits → Fin b.bits}
    (hP : IsPermBy P τ) (σ : Fin b.bits → Fin c.bits) (h₁ : ∀ j, σ (τ j) = j)
    (h₂ : ∀ i, τ (σ i) = i) (f : Hom a b) (x : Fin a.bits → ZMod 2) (z : Fin c.bits → ZMod 2) :
    entry (comp f P) x z = entry f x (z ∘ σ) := by
  unfold IsPermBy at hP
  simp only [entry_comp, hP]
  simp only [eq_comp_iff (u := z) h₁ h₂, mul_ite, mul_one, mul_zero, Finset.sum_ite_eq',
    Finset.mem_univ, if_true]

/-! ### The symmetry's laws -/

/-- **The symmetry is an involution**. Proved at T46.3.2. -/
theorem swap_swap (a b : Obj) : comp (swap a b) (swap b a) = id (tensorObj a b) := by
  exact perm_eq (isPermBy_comp (isPermBy_swap a b) (isPermBy_swap b a)) (isPermBy_id _)
    (fun j => by rw [swapIndex_swapIndex])

/-- **The symmetry is natural**: swapping after a tensor is tensoring in the other order after a
swap. Proved at T46.3.2. -/
theorem swap_natural {a b a' b' : Obj} (f : Hom a b) (g : Hom a' b') :
    comp (tensor f g) (swap b b') = comp (swap a a') (tensor g f) := by
  refine hom_ext fun u w => ?_
  rw [entry_comp_perm_right (isPermBy_swap b b') (swapIndex b'.bits b.bits)
      (swapIndex_swapIndex _ _) (swapIndex_swapIndex _ _),
    entry_comp_perm_left (isPermBy_swap a a'), entry_tensor, entry_tensor, mul_comm]
  congr 2 <;> funext j <;> simp only [Function.comp_apply] <;> congr 1 <;> ext <;>
    have := j.isLt <;> simp only [val_swapIndex, Fin.val_castAdd, Fin.val_natAdd] <;>
    (try split_ifs) <;> omega

/-- **The hexagon**: the symmetry of a tensor against a third object is the two symmetries of its
factors in turn, through the casts of `Nat.add_assoc`. Proved at T46.3.2. -/
theorem swap_hexagon (a b c : Obj) :
    swap (tensorObj a b) c
      = comp
          (castHom (Nat.add_assoc a.bits b.bits c.bits).symm
            (Nat.add_assoc a.bits c.bits b.bits).symm (tensor (id a) (swap b c)))
          (castHom rfl (Nat.add_assoc c.bits a.bits b.bits) (tensor (swap a c) (id b))) := by
  refine perm_eq (isPermBy_swap _ _) (isPermBy_comp
    (isPermBy_castHom _ _ (isPermBy_tensor (isPermBy_id a) (isPermBy_swap b c)))
    (isPermBy_castHom _ _ (isPermBy_tensor (isPermBy_swap a c) (isPermBy_id b)))) fun j => ?_
  simp only [val_swapIndex, Fin.val_cast, val_append_index, Fin.val_castAdd, Fin.val_natAdd,
    tensorObj]
  split_ifs <;> omega

/-! ### The tensor's laws on morphisms -/

/-- **The tensor is associative on morphisms**: `(f ⊗ g) ⊗ h`, read through the casts of
`Nat.add_assoc` on its inputs and its outputs, is `f ⊗ (g ⊗ h)`. Proved at T46.3.2. -/
theorem tensor_assoc {a₁ b₁ a₂ b₂ a₃ b₃ : Obj} (f : Hom a₁ b₁) (g : Hom a₂ b₂) (h : Hom a₃ b₃) :
    castHom (a' := tensorObj a₁ (tensorObj a₂ a₃)) (b' := tensorObj b₁ (tensorObj b₂ b₃))
        (Nat.add_assoc a₁.bits a₂.bits a₃.bits) (Nat.add_assoc b₁.bits b₂.bits b₃.bits)
        (tensor (tensor f g) h)
      = tensor f (tensor g h) := by
  refine hom_ext fun x y => ?_
  rw [entry_castHom]
  erw [entry_tensor, entry_tensor]
  rw [entry_tensor, entry_tensor, mul_assoc]
  refine congrArg₂ (· * ·) (entry_congr ?_ ?_)
    (congrArg₂ (· * ·) (entry_congr ?_ ?_) (entry_congr ?_ ?_)) <;> funext j <;>
    simp only [Function.comp_apply] <;>
    (first | refine congrArg x (Fin.ext ?_) | refine congrArg y (Fin.ext ?_)) <;>
    simp only [Fin.val_cast, Fin.val_castAdd, Fin.val_natAdd] <;> omega

/-- **The empty register is a left unit for the tensor on morphisms**: `id_0 ⊗ f`, read through the
casts of `Nat.zero_add`, is `f`. Proved at T46.3.2. -/
theorem tensor_id_left {a b : Obj} (f : Hom a b) :
    castHom (a' := a) (b' := b) (Nat.zero_add a.bits) (Nat.zero_add b.bits)
        (tensor (FrameCategory.id ⟨0⟩) f)
      = f := by
  refine hom_ext fun x y => ?_
  rw [entry_castHom]
  erw [entry_tensor]
  rw [entry_id, if_pos (Subsingleton.elim _ _), one_mul]
  refine entry_congr ?_ ?_ <;> funext j <;> simp only [Function.comp_apply] <;>
    (first | refine congrArg x (Fin.ext ?_) | refine congrArg y (Fin.ext ?_)) <;>
    simp only [Fin.val_cast, Fin.val_natAdd, Nat.zero_add]

/-- **The empty register is a right unit for the tensor on morphisms**: `f ⊗ id_0`, read through
the casts of `Nat.add_zero`, is `f`. Proved at T46.3.2. -/
theorem tensor_id_right {a b : Obj} (f : Hom a b) :
    castHom (a' := a) (b' := b) (Nat.add_zero a.bits) (Nat.add_zero b.bits)
        (tensor f (FrameCategory.id ⟨0⟩))
      = f := by
  refine hom_ext fun x y => ?_
  rw [entry_castHom]
  erw [entry_tensor]
  rw [entry_id, if_pos (Subsingleton.elim _ _), mul_one]
  refine entry_congr ?_ ?_ <;> funext j <;> simp only [Function.comp_apply] <;>
    (first | refine congrArg x (Fin.ext ?_) | refine congrArg y (Fin.ext ?_)) <;>
    simp only [Fin.val_cast, Fin.val_castAdd]

/-! ## The Mathlib instances

The tensor's associativity and units on morphisms (`tensor_assoc`, `tensor_id_left`,
`tensor_id_right`) and the instances were added to the frozen statement by an additions-only
restatement (docs/STEPS.md, entry 2026-10-01p; `docs/decisions/T46.md`). The associator and the
unitors are casts of identities (`castHom`), since the objects add strictly. -/

/-! ### The structure maps and the laws the Mathlib instances name

Restated by entry 2026-10-02b (docs/STEPS.md): every proof field of the three instances names a
theorem here, so that no definition's value holds `sorry` and proving a law never moves the
statement hash. The structure maps are the instances' own data, named. The inverse laws and the
whiskering identities are proved at T46.3.2, the coherence at T46.3.4, its proofs on index maps
given by the laws themselves (entry 2026-10-02e: each had a private twin before). -/

/-- The associator `(a ⊗ b) ⊗ c → a ⊗ (b ⊗ c)`: the identity cast along `Nat.add_assoc`. -/
noncomputable def associatorHom (a b c : Obj) :
    Hom (tensorObj (tensorObj a b) c) (tensorObj a (tensorObj b c)) :=
  castHom (a' := tensorObj (tensorObj a b) c) (b' := tensorObj a (tensorObj b c)) rfl
    (Nat.add_assoc a.bits b.bits c.bits) (FrameCategory.id (tensorObj (tensorObj a b) c))

/-- The associator's inverse `a ⊗ (b ⊗ c) → (a ⊗ b) ⊗ c`. -/
noncomputable def associatorInv (a b c : Obj) :
    Hom (tensorObj a (tensorObj b c)) (tensorObj (tensorObj a b) c) :=
  castHom (a' := tensorObj a (tensorObj b c)) (b' := tensorObj (tensorObj a b) c) rfl
    (Nat.add_assoc a.bits b.bits c.bits).symm (FrameCategory.id (tensorObj a (tensorObj b c)))

/-- The left unitor `0 ⊗ a → a`: the identity cast along `Nat.zero_add`. -/
noncomputable def leftUnitorHom (a : Obj) : Hom (tensorObj ⟨0⟩ a) a :=
  castHom (a' := tensorObj ⟨0⟩ a) (b' := a) rfl (Nat.zero_add a.bits)
    (FrameCategory.id (tensorObj ⟨0⟩ a))

/-- The left unitor's inverse `a → 0 ⊗ a`. -/
noncomputable def leftUnitorInv (a : Obj) : Hom a (tensorObj ⟨0⟩ a) :=
  castHom (a' := a) (b' := tensorObj ⟨0⟩ a) rfl (Nat.zero_add a.bits).symm (FrameCategory.id a)

/-- The right unitor `a ⊗ 0 → a`: the identity cast along `Nat.add_zero`. -/
noncomputable def rightUnitorHom (a : Obj) : Hom (tensorObj a ⟨0⟩) a :=
  castHom (a' := tensorObj a ⟨0⟩) (b' := a) rfl (Nat.add_zero a.bits)
    (FrameCategory.id (tensorObj a ⟨0⟩))

/-- The right unitor's inverse `a → a ⊗ 0`. -/
noncomputable def rightUnitorInv (a : Obj) : Hom a (tensorObj a ⟨0⟩) :=
  castHom (a' := a) (b' := tensorObj a ⟨0⟩) rfl (Nat.add_zero a.bits).symm (FrameCategory.id a)

/-! ### The fields of the Mathlib instances -/

/-- A cast of an identity is a permutation morphism. -/
private theorem isPermBy_castId {a a' b' : Obj} (h₁ : a.bits = a'.bits) (h₂ : a.bits = b'.bits) :
    IsPermBy (castHom (a' := a') (b' := b') h₁ h₂ (FrameCategory.id a))
      (fun j => Fin.cast h₁ (Fin.cast h₂.symm j)) :=
  isPermBy_castHom h₁ h₂ (isPermBy_id a)

/-- Two casts are one. -/
private theorem castHom_castHom {a b a' b' a'' b'' : Obj} (h₁ : a'.bits = a''.bits)
    (h₂ : b'.bits = b''.bits) (h₃ : a.bits = a'.bits) (h₄ : b.bits = b'.bits) (f : Hom a b) :
    castHom h₁ h₂ (castHom h₃ h₄ f) = castHom (h₃.trans h₁) (h₄.trans h₂) f :=
  hom_ext fun x y => by
    rw [entry_castHom, entry_castHom, entry_castHom]
    rfl

/-- Composing with a cast identity on the right casts the output. -/
private theorem comp_castId {a b b' c : Obj} (f : Hom a b') (h₁ : b.bits = b'.bits)
    (h₂ : b.bits = c.bits) :
    comp f (castHom (a' := b') (b' := c) h₁ h₂ (FrameCategory.id b))
      = castHom (a' := a) (b' := c) rfl (h₁.symm.trans h₂) f :=
  hom_ext fun x z => by
    rw [entry_comp_perm_right (isPermBy_castId h₁ h₂) (fun i => Fin.cast h₂ (Fin.cast h₁.symm i))
      (fun j => Fin.ext rfl) (fun i => Fin.ext rfl), entry_castHom]
    rfl

/-- Composing with a cast identity on the left casts the input. -/
private theorem castId_comp {a a' b' c : Obj} (h₁ : a.bits = a'.bits) (h₂ : a.bits = b'.bits)
    (g : Hom b' c) :
    comp (castHom (a' := a') (b' := b') h₁ h₂ (FrameCategory.id a)) g
      = castHom (a' := a') (b' := c) (h₂.symm.trans h₁) rfl g :=
  hom_ext fun x z => by
    rw [entry_comp_perm_left (isPermBy_castId h₁ h₂), entry_castHom]
    rfl

/-- **The associator is natural**. Proved at T46.3.4. -/
theorem associator_naturality {X₁ X₂ X₃ Y₁ Y₂ Y₃ : Obj} (f₁ : Hom X₁ Y₁)
    (f₂ : Hom X₂ Y₂) (f₃ : Hom X₃ Y₃) :
    comp (tensor (tensor f₁ f₂) f₃) (associatorHom Y₁ Y₂ Y₃)
      = comp (associatorHom X₁ X₂ X₃) (tensor f₁ (tensor f₂ f₃)) := by
  unfold associatorHom
  erw [comp_castId, castId_comp]
  rw [← tensor_assoc, castHom_castHom]
  rfl

/-- **The left unitor is natural**. Proved at T46.3.4. -/
theorem leftUnitor_naturality {X Y : Obj} (f : Hom X Y) :
    comp (tensor (FrameCategory.id ⟨0⟩) f) (leftUnitorHom Y) = comp (leftUnitorHom X) f := by
  unfold leftUnitorHom
  erw [comp_castId, castId_comp]
  conv_rhs => rw [← tensor_id_left f]
  rw [castHom_castHom]
  rfl

/-- **The right unitor is natural**. Proved at T46.3.4. -/
theorem rightUnitor_naturality {X Y : Obj} (f : Hom X Y) :
    comp (tensor f (FrameCategory.id ⟨0⟩)) (rightUnitorHom Y) = comp (rightUnitorHom X) f := by
  unfold rightUnitorHom
  erw [comp_castId, castId_comp]
  conv_rhs => rw [← tensor_id_right f]
  rw [castHom_castHom]
  rfl

/-- **The pentagon**. Proved at T46.3.4. -/
theorem pentagon (W X Y Z : Obj) :
    comp (tensor (associatorHom W X Y) (FrameCategory.id Z))
        (comp (associatorHom W (tensorObj X Y) Z)
          (tensor (FrameCategory.id W) (associatorHom X Y Z)))
      = comp (associatorHom (tensorObj W X) Y Z) (associatorHom W X (tensorObj Y Z)) := by
  refine perm_eq (isPermBy_comp (isPermBy_tensor (isPermBy_castId _ _) (isPermBy_id _))
    (isPermBy_comp (isPermBy_castId _ _) (isPermBy_tensor (isPermBy_id _) (isPermBy_castId _ _))))
    (isPermBy_comp (isPermBy_castId _ _) (isPermBy_castId _ _)) fun j => ?_
  have := j.isLt
  simp only [tensorObj] at this
  simp only [Fin.val_cast, val_append_index, Fin.val_castAdd, Fin.val_natAdd, tensorObj]
  split_ifs <;> omega

/-- **The triangle**. Proved at T46.3.4. -/
theorem triangle (X Y : Obj) :
    comp (associatorHom X ⟨0⟩ Y) (tensor (FrameCategory.id X) (leftUnitorHom Y))
      = tensor (rightUnitorHom X) (FrameCategory.id Y) := by
  refine perm_eq (isPermBy_comp (isPermBy_castId _ _)
    (isPermBy_tensor (isPermBy_id _) (isPermBy_castId _ _)))
    (isPermBy_tensor (isPermBy_castId _ _) (isPermBy_id _)) fun j => ?_
  have := j.isLt
  simp only [tensorObj] at this
  simp only [Fin.val_cast, val_append_index, Fin.val_castAdd, Fin.val_natAdd, tensorObj]
  split_ifs <;> omega

/-- **The first hexagon**, in Mathlib's form. Proved at T46.3.4. -/
theorem hexagon_forward (X Y Z : Obj) :
    comp (associatorHom X Y Z) (comp (swap X (tensorObj Y Z)) (associatorHom Y Z X))
      = comp (tensor (swap X Y) (FrameCategory.id Z))
          (comp (associatorHom Y X Z) (tensor (FrameCategory.id Y) (swap X Z))) := by
  refine perm_eq (isPermBy_comp (isPermBy_castId _ _)
    (isPermBy_comp (isPermBy_swap _ _) (isPermBy_castId _ _)))
    (isPermBy_comp (isPermBy_tensor (isPermBy_swap _ _) (isPermBy_id _))
      (isPermBy_comp (isPermBy_castId _ _) (isPermBy_tensor (isPermBy_id _) (isPermBy_swap _ _))))
    fun j => ?_
  have := j.isLt
  simp only [tensorObj] at this
  simp only [val_swapIndex, Fin.val_cast, val_append_index, Fin.val_castAdd, Fin.val_natAdd,
    tensorObj]
  split_ifs <;> omega

/-- **The second hexagon**, in Mathlib's form. Proved at T46.3.4. -/
theorem hexagon_reverse (X Y Z : Obj) :
    comp (associatorInv X Y Z) (comp (swap (tensorObj X Y) Z) (associatorInv Z X Y))
      = comp (tensor (FrameCategory.id X) (swap Y Z))
          (comp (associatorInv X Z Y) (tensor (swap X Z) (FrameCategory.id Y))) := by
  refine perm_eq (isPermBy_comp (isPermBy_castId _ _)
    (isPermBy_comp (isPermBy_swap _ _) (isPermBy_castId _ _)))
    (isPermBy_comp (isPermBy_tensor (isPermBy_id _) (isPermBy_swap _ _))
      (isPermBy_comp (isPermBy_castId _ _) (isPermBy_tensor (isPermBy_swap _ _) (isPermBy_id _))))
    fun j => ?_
  have := j.isLt
  simp only [tensorObj] at this
  simp only [val_swapIndex, Fin.val_cast, val_append_index, Fin.val_castAdd, Fin.val_natAdd,
    tensorObj]
  split_ifs <;> omega

/-- The associator followed by its inverse is the identity. Proved at T46.3.2. -/
theorem associator_hom_inv_id (a b c : Obj) :
    comp (associatorHom a b c) (associatorInv a b c)
      = FrameCategory.id (tensorObj (tensorObj a b) c) :=
  perm_eq (isPermBy_comp (isPermBy_castId _ _) (isPermBy_castId _ _)) (isPermBy_id _)
    fun _ => rfl

/-- The associator's inverse followed by the associator is the identity. Proved at T46.3.2. -/
theorem associator_inv_hom_id (a b c : Obj) :
    comp (associatorInv a b c) (associatorHom a b c)
      = FrameCategory.id (tensorObj a (tensorObj b c)) :=
  perm_eq (isPermBy_comp (isPermBy_castId _ _) (isPermBy_castId _ _)) (isPermBy_id _)
    fun _ => rfl

/-- The left unitor followed by its inverse is the identity. Proved at T46.3.2. -/
theorem leftUnitor_hom_inv_id (a : Obj) :
    comp (leftUnitorHom a) (leftUnitorInv a) = FrameCategory.id (tensorObj ⟨0⟩ a) :=
  perm_eq (isPermBy_comp (isPermBy_castId _ _) (isPermBy_castId _ _)) (isPermBy_id _)
    fun _ => rfl

/-- The left unitor's inverse followed by the left unitor is the identity. Proved at T46.3.2. -/
theorem leftUnitor_inv_hom_id (a : Obj) :
    comp (leftUnitorInv a) (leftUnitorHom a) = FrameCategory.id a :=
  perm_eq (isPermBy_comp (isPermBy_castId _ _) (isPermBy_castId _ _)) (isPermBy_id _)
    fun _ => rfl

/-- The right unitor followed by its inverse is the identity. Proved at T46.3.2. -/
theorem rightUnitor_hom_inv_id (a : Obj) :
    comp (rightUnitorHom a) (rightUnitorInv a) = FrameCategory.id (tensorObj a ⟨0⟩) :=
  perm_eq (isPermBy_comp (isPermBy_castId _ _) (isPermBy_castId _ _)) (isPermBy_id _)
    fun _ => rfl

/-- The right unitor's inverse followed by the right unitor is the identity. Proved at T46.3.2. -/
theorem rightUnitor_inv_hom_id (a : Obj) :
    comp (rightUnitorInv a) (rightUnitorHom a) = FrameCategory.id a :=
  perm_eq (isPermBy_comp (isPermBy_castId _ _) (isPermBy_castId _ _)) (isPermBy_id _)
    fun _ => rfl

/-- The tensor of morphisms is the right whiskering followed by the left:
`f ⊗ g = (f ⊗ 1) ≫ (1 ⊗ g)`. Proved at T46.3.2. -/
theorem tensorHom_def {a₁ b₁ a₂ b₂ : Obj} (f : Hom a₁ b₁) (g : Hom a₂ b₂) :
    tensor f g = comp (tensor f (FrameCategory.id a₂)) (tensor (FrameCategory.id b₁) g) := by
  rw [← tensor_comp, comp_id, id_comp]

/-- The composite of two tensors is the tensor of the composites, in Mathlib's orientation:
`tensor_comp` read right to left. Proved at T46.3.2. -/
theorem tensorHom_comp_tensorHom {a₁ b₁ c₁ a₂ b₂ c₂ : Obj} (f₁ : Hom a₁ b₁) (f₂ : Hom a₂ b₂)
    (g₁ : Hom b₁ c₁) (g₂ : Hom b₂ c₂) :
    comp (tensor f₁ f₂) (tensor g₁ g₂) = tensor (comp f₁ g₁) (comp f₂ g₂) :=
  (tensor_comp f₁ g₁ f₂ g₂).symm

-- designed double: tensor_id, id_whiskerRight (Mathlib's field name; entry 2026-10-02d)
/-- Left whiskering by an identity is the identity. Proved at T46.3.2. -/
theorem whiskerLeft_id (a b : Obj) :
    tensor (FrameCategory.id a) (FrameCategory.id b) = FrameCategory.id (tensorObj a b) :=
  tensor_id a b

-- designed double: tensor_id, whiskerLeft_id (Mathlib's field name; entry 2026-10-02d)
/-- Right whiskering of an identity is the identity. Proved at T46.3.2. -/
theorem id_whiskerRight (a b : Obj) :
    tensor (FrameCategory.id a) (FrameCategory.id b) = FrameCategory.id (tensorObj a b) :=
  tensor_id a b

/-- **The braiding is natural on the right**. Proved at T46.3.4. -/
theorem braiding_naturality_right (a : Obj) {b c : Obj} (f : Hom b c) :
    comp (tensor (FrameCategory.id a) f) (swap a c)
      = comp (swap a b) (tensor f (FrameCategory.id a)) :=
  swap_natural (FrameCategory.id a) f

/-- **The braiding is natural on the left**. Proved at T46.3.4. -/
theorem braiding_naturality_left {a b : Obj} (f : Hom a b) (c : Obj) :
    comp (tensor f (FrameCategory.id c)) (swap b c)
      = comp (swap a c) (tensor (FrameCategory.id c) f) :=
  swap_natural f (FrameCategory.id c)

/-- **The frame as a Mathlib category**: the classes as morphisms, `FrameCategory.comp` as `≫`
(diagrammatic, as Mathlib's), `FrameCategory.id` as `𝟙`; its laws are `comp_assoc`, `id_comp` and
`comp_id`. -/
noncomputable instance category : CategoryTheory.Category Obj where
  Hom := Hom
  id := FrameCategory.id
  comp := FrameCategory.comp
  id_comp := FrameCategory.id_comp
  comp_id := FrameCategory.comp_id
  assoc := FrameCategory.comp_assoc

/-- **The frame as a Mathlib monoidal category**: the tensor of objects and of morphisms, the
whiskerings as tensors with an identity, the unit the empty register, and the associator and the
unitors the casts of identities along `Nat.add_assoc`, `Nat.zero_add` and `Nat.add_zero`. Its
laws are proved at T46.3.2. -/
noncomputable instance monoidalCategory : CategoryTheory.MonoidalCategory Obj where
  tensorObj := tensorObj
  whiskerLeft X _ _ f := tensor (FrameCategory.id X) f
  whiskerRight f Y := tensor f (FrameCategory.id Y)
  tensorHom f g := tensor f g
  tensorUnit := ⟨0⟩
  associator a b c :=
    { hom := castHom (a' := tensorObj (tensorObj a b) c) (b' := tensorObj a (tensorObj b c)) rfl
        (Nat.add_assoc a.bits b.bits c.bits) (FrameCategory.id (tensorObj (tensorObj a b) c))
      inv := castHom (a' := tensorObj a (tensorObj b c)) (b' := tensorObj (tensorObj a b) c) rfl
        (Nat.add_assoc a.bits b.bits c.bits).symm (FrameCategory.id (tensorObj a (tensorObj b c)))
      hom_inv_id := FrameCategory.associator_hom_inv_id a b c
      inv_hom_id := FrameCategory.associator_inv_hom_id a b c }
  leftUnitor a :=
    { hom := castHom (a' := tensorObj ⟨0⟩ a) (b' := a) rfl (Nat.zero_add a.bits)
        (FrameCategory.id (tensorObj ⟨0⟩ a))
      inv := castHom (a' := a) (b' := tensorObj ⟨0⟩ a) rfl (Nat.zero_add a.bits).symm
        (FrameCategory.id a)
      hom_inv_id := FrameCategory.leftUnitor_hom_inv_id a
      inv_hom_id := FrameCategory.leftUnitor_inv_hom_id a }
  rightUnitor a :=
    { hom := castHom (a' := tensorObj a ⟨0⟩) (b' := a) rfl (Nat.add_zero a.bits)
        (FrameCategory.id (tensorObj a ⟨0⟩))
      inv := castHom (a' := a) (b' := tensorObj a ⟨0⟩) rfl (Nat.add_zero a.bits).symm
        (FrameCategory.id a)
      hom_inv_id := FrameCategory.rightUnitor_hom_inv_id a
      inv_hom_id := FrameCategory.rightUnitor_inv_hom_id a }
  tensorHom_def := FrameCategory.tensorHom_def
  id_tensorHom_id := tensor_id
  tensorHom_comp_tensorHom := FrameCategory.tensorHom_comp_tensorHom
  whiskerLeft_id := FrameCategory.whiskerLeft_id
  id_whiskerRight := FrameCategory.id_whiskerRight
  associator_naturality := FrameCategory.associator_naturality
  leftUnitor_naturality := FrameCategory.leftUnitor_naturality
  rightUnitor_naturality := FrameCategory.rightUnitor_naturality
  pentagon := FrameCategory.pentagon
  triangle := FrameCategory.triangle

/-- **The frame as a Mathlib symmetric monoidal category**: the braiding is the symmetry `swap`,
its own inverse by `swap_swap`; naturality and the hexagons are the theorems above, proved
at T46.3.4. -/
noncomputable instance symmetricCategory : CategoryTheory.SymmetricCategory Obj where
  braiding a b :=
    { hom := swap a b
      inv := swap b a
      hom_inv_id := swap_swap a b
      inv_hom_id := swap_swap b a }
  braiding_naturality_right := FrameCategory.braiding_naturality_right
  braiding_naturality_left := FrameCategory.braiding_naturality_left
  hexagon_forward := FrameCategory.hexagon_forward
  hexagon_reverse := FrameCategory.hexagon_reverse
  symmetry := swap_swap

/-! ## States and T14's terms as morphisms -/

/-- **A carrier state as a morphism** `0 → n`, through the cast `0 + n = n`, which keeps `amp`. -/
noncomputable def ofState {n : ℕ} (S : KernelSumState n) : Hom ⟨0⟩ ⟨n⟩ :=
  toHom (castBits (Nat.zero_add n).symm S)

/-- Two states give one morphism exactly when they are `StateEq`: the embedding is injective on
classes, since the cast keeps `amp` and `Fin.cast` is a bijection of the words. -/
theorem ofState_inj {n : ℕ} (S T : KernelSumState n) : ofState S = ofState T ↔ StateEq S T := by
  rw [ofState, ofState, toHom_eq_toHom_iff]
  unfold StateEq
  rw [amp_castBits, amp_castBits]
  constructor
  · intro h
    funext u
    exact congrFun h (u ∘ Fin.cast (Nat.zero_add n))
  · intro h
    rw [h]

/-- **A gate word as a morphism** `N → N`, at its precision. -/
noncomputable def wordHom (N M : ℕ) (w : GateWord N M) : Hom ⟨N⟩ ⟨N⟩ := toHom (wordState N M w)

/-- **A conditioning letter as a morphism** `N → N + 1`, at the protocol's precision. -/
noncomputable def conditionHom (N M : ℕ) (P : SignedPauli N) : Hom ⟨N⟩ ⟨N + 1⟩ :=
  toHom (conditionState N M P)

/-- **A protocol as a morphism** `N → N + k`: the composite of its letters' morphisms in order,
the empty protocol the identity. The codomains `N + (k + 1)` and `(N + k) + 1` agree by
definition, so no cast is needed. -/
noncomputable def protocolHom {M N : ℕ} : {k : ℕ} → Protocol M N k → Hom ⟨N⟩ ⟨N + k⟩
  | _, .nil => id ⟨N⟩
  | _, .word p w => comp (protocolHom p) (wordHom _ M w)
  | _, .condition p P _ => comp (protocolHom p) (conditionHom _ M P)

@[simp] theorem protocolHom_nil {M N : ℕ} : protocolHom (.nil : Protocol M N 0) = id ⟨N⟩ :=
  rfl

@[simp] theorem protocolHom_word {M N k : ℕ} (p : Protocol M N k) (w : GateWord (N + k) M) :
    protocolHom (p.word w) = comp (protocolHom p) (wordHom (N + k) M w) :=
  rfl

@[simp] theorem protocolHom_condition {M N k : ℕ} (p : Protocol M N k) (P : SignedPauli (N + k))
    (hP : yWeight P.pauli % 2 = 1 → 2 ≤ M) :
    protocolHom (p.condition P hP) = comp (protocolHom p) (conditionHom (N + k) M P) :=
  rfl

/-! ### T14's terms as composites

`interpret_eq_comp` follows the referees `amp_comp`, `amp_wordState` and `amp_conditionState`,
which it needs; it was stated above them, after `protocolHom`, and moved here at T46.3.3 with its
name, type and docstring unchanged. A theorem's position is outside the statement hash
(tools/gate/gate.py, `statement_hash`, which reads a value only of a definition). -/

/-- An amplitude function is the sum of its values times the point masses. -/
private theorem sum_smul_delta {N : ℕ} (g : (Fin N → ZMod 2) → ℂ) :
    ∑ v, g v • delta v = g := by
  funext u
  rw [Finset.sum_apply]
  simp only [Pi.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul, delta, mul_ite, mul_one, mul_zero, Finset.sum_ite_eq,
    Finset.mem_univ, if_true]

/-- Summing an amplitude function against the point masses read at `u` gives its value at `u`. -/
private theorem sum_mul_delta {N : ℕ} (g : (Fin N → ZMod 2) → ℂ) (u : Fin N → ZMod 2) :
    ∑ v, g v * delta v u = g u := by
  simp only [delta, mul_ite, mul_one, mul_zero, Finset.sum_ite_eq, Finset.mem_univ, if_true]

/-- A word's referee sends the zero function to zero, by `runAmp_add_smul` at `0 + 1 • 0`. -/
private theorem runAmp_zero_function {N M : ℕ} (W : GateWord N M) : runAmp W 0 = 0 := by
  have h := runAmp_add_smul W 0 0 1
  rw [smul_zero, add_zero, one_smul] at h
  exact add_eq_left.mp h.symm

/-- A word's referee of a finite combination of point masses is the combination of its referees. -/
private theorem runAmp_sum_smul_delta {N M : ℕ} (W : GateWord N M)
    (s : Finset (Fin N → ZMod 2)) (c : (Fin N → ZMod 2) → ℂ) :
    runAmp W (∑ v ∈ s, c v • delta v) = ∑ v ∈ s, c v • runAmp W (delta v) := by
  induction s using Finset.induction_on with
  | empty => rw [Finset.sum_empty, Finset.sum_empty, runAmp_zero_function]
  | insert v s hv ih =>
    rw [Finset.sum_insert hv, Finset.sum_insert hv, add_comm, runAmp_add_smul, ih, add_comm]

/-- **A word's referee is determined by its values on point masses**, by `runAmp_add_smul`. -/
private theorem runAmp_eq_sum_delta {N M : ℕ} (W : GateWord N M) (g : (Fin N → ZMod 2) → ℂ)
    (y : Fin N → ZMod 2) : runAmp W g y = ∑ v, g v * runAmp W (delta v) y := by
  conv_lhs => rw [← sum_smul_delta g]
  rw [runAmp_sum_smul_delta, Finset.sum_apply]
  simp only [Pi.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul]

/-- **The projection is determined by its values on point masses**, by `pauliProjection_apply`. -/
private theorem pauliProjection_eq_sum_delta {N : ℕ} (P : SignedPauli N) (b : ZMod 2)
    (g : (Fin N → ZMod 2) → ℂ) (z : Fin N → ZMod 2) :
    pauliProjection P b g z = ∑ v, g v * pauliProjection P b (delta v) z := by
  have hterm : ∀ v, g v * pauliProjection P b (delta v) z
      = 1 / 2 * (g v * delta v z)
        + 1 / 2 * shiftFactor P b z * (g v * delta v (z + P.pauli.X)) := by
    intro v
    rw [pauliProjection_apply]
    ring
  rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl fun v _ => hterm v, Finset.sum_add_distrib, ← Finset.mul_sum,
    ← Finset.mul_sum, sum_mul_delta, sum_mul_delta, pauliProjection_apply]
  ring

/-- The entry of a state's morphism `0 → n` at the output `y` is the state's amplitude at `y`. -/
private theorem entry_ofState {n : ℕ} (S : KernelSumState n) (x : Fin (⟨0⟩ : Obj).bits → ZMod 2)
    (y : Fin (⟨n⟩ : Obj).bits → ZMod 2) : entry (ofState S) x y = amp S y := by
  change amp (castBits (Nat.zero_add n).symm S) (Fin.append x y) = amp S y
  rw [amp_castBits]
  beta_reduce
  congr 1
  funext i
  have hi : Fin.cast (Nat.zero_add n).symm i = Fin.natAdd 0 i :=
    Fin.ext (by simp only [Fin.val_cast, Fin.val_natAdd, Nat.zero_add])
  rw [Function.comp_apply, hi, Fin.append_right]

/-- The entry of a word's morphism at `(x, y)` is the word's referee on the point mass at `x`. -/
private theorem entry_wordHom (N M : ℕ) (w : GateWord N M) (hM : 1 ≤ M)
    (x : Fin (⟨N⟩ : Obj).bits → ZMod 2) (y : Fin (⟨N⟩ : Obj).bits → ZMod 2) :
    entry (wordHom N M w) x y = runAmp w (delta x) y :=
  amp_wordState N M w hM x y

/-- The entry of a conditioning letter's morphism at `(x, y)` is the projection, at the outcome
`y`'s last bit, of the point mass at `x`, read at the rest of `y`. -/
private theorem entry_conditionHom (N M : ℕ) (P : SignedPauli N)
    (x : Fin (⟨N⟩ : Obj).bits → ZMod 2) (y : Fin (⟨N + 1⟩ : Obj).bits → ZMod 2) :
    entry (conditionHom N M P) x y = pauliProjection P (y (Fin.last N)) (delta x) (Fin.init y) := by
  change amp (conditionState N M P) (Fin.append x y) = _
  conv_lhs => rw [← Fin.snoc_init_self y]
  exact amp_conditionState N M P x (Fin.init y) (y (Fin.last N))

/-- **T14's referee is the protocol's morphism read as a matrix**: at a positive precision,
`interpretAmp p f` at `y` is `Σ_u f(u)·⟨y|p|u⟩`, letter by letter, by `runAmp_eq_sum_delta` and
`pauliProjection_eq_sum_delta`. -/
private theorem interpretAmp_eq_sum_entry {M N k : ℕ} (hM : 1 ≤ M) (p : Protocol M N k)
    (f : (Fin N → ZMod 2) → ℂ) :
    p.interpretAmp f = fun y => ∑ u, f u * entry (protocolHom p) u y := by
  induction p with
  | nil =>
    rw [Protocol.interpretAmp_nil, protocolHom_nil]
    funext y
    simp only [entry_id, mul_ite, mul_one, mul_zero, Finset.sum_ite_eq, Finset.mem_univ, if_true]
  | word p w ih =>
    rw [Protocol.interpretAmp_word, protocolHom_word, ih]
    funext y
    rw [runAmp_eq_sum_delta]
    simp only [entry_comp, entry_wordHom _ M w hM, Finset.sum_mul, Finset.mul_sum, mul_assoc]
    exact Finset.sum_comm
  | condition p P hP ih =>
    rw [Protocol.interpretAmp_condition, protocolHom_condition, ih]
    funext y
    rw [pauliProjection_eq_sum_delta]
    simp only [entry_comp, entry_conditionHom, Finset.sum_mul, Finset.mul_sum, mul_assoc]
    exact Finset.sum_comm

/-- **T14's interpretation is the composite of its letters' morphisms.** On a carrier state `S` at
the protocol's precision (the hypotheses of `amp_interpret`), the class of `interpret p S`, as a
morphism from `0`, is `S` composed with the protocol's morphism, letter by letter: `interpretAmp`
is linear in the input, by linearity of `runAmp` and of `pauliProjection`, so it is determined by
its values on point masses, which `amp_wordState` and `amp_conditionState` give. Proved at
T46.3.3. -/
theorem interpret_eq_comp {M N k : ℕ} (p : Protocol M N k) {S : KernelSumState N}
    (hS : IsCarrier S) (hm : S.m = M) :
    ofState (p.interpret S) = comp (ofState S) (protocolHom p) := by
  have hM : 1 ≤ M := hm ▸ hS.1
  refine hom_ext fun x y => ?_
  rw [entry_ofState, (amp_interpret p hS hm).2, interpretAmp_eq_sum_entry hM p, entry_comp]
  exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun u _ => by rw [entry_ofState]

end FrameCategory

end FTQCLib.Frame.Walkthrough
